      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "Among the Anishinaabeg (Ojibwe, Odawa, Potawatomi) the underwater panther — Mishipeshu, \"the Great Lynx\" — is a composite: the body of a wild cat, horns of deer or bison, upright scales along the back, an immensely long tail. It lives in deep water, raises storms, squalls and rapids, drowns people, and is master of water creatures including snakes; it is the counter-power to the Thunderbirds.",
