      "synopsis": "Original note includes uncertainty or estimates: La Salle's Griffon, keel laid 26 Jan 1679 above Niagara and the first sailing ship on the upper lakes, sailed from the Green Bay islands on 18 Sept 1679 with some 12,000 pounds of furs worth 50–60,000 francs and vanished with all hands. La Salle suspected the pilot, Luc (the Dane), of scuttling her and deserting with the furs to join Du Lhut, and hinted that rival traders and the Jesuits covered it up.",
