      "summary": "Reported sightings include: 1793, the captain of the sloop Bay Rat near Sandusky, a creature \"more than a rod\" (16½ ft) long; July 1817, a schooner crew's 30–40-ft dark serpent; later in 1817 another crew's copper-coloured 60-footer, which they fired on with muskets to no effect; also 1817, the Dusseau brothers near Toledo found on the beach a 20–30-ft creature shaped like a sturgeon but with arms, which left silver scales behind; July 1892, a ship's crew on the Buffalo–Toledo run reported a 50-ft animal 4 ft round, \"carried by local newspapers\"; 5 May 1896, four witnesses at Crystal Beach watched a 30-ft creature with a \"dog-shaped head and pointy tail\" for 45 minutes. The nickname \"Bessie\"/\"South Bay Bessie\" is not dated on the page — treat it as later. The odd detail: The 1817 beast had arms and shed silver scales — silver, the werewolf metal, from a lake monster.",
