          "label": "Proposal — historical sense",
          "text": "French Guiana not sold — no American Congress will vote dollars for a penal colony, and France will not give up its dumping ground. It stays French and stays a bagne into the 1930s, on the border of American-bought British Guiana (if Part E's proposal stands). Its escapees become an American problem: every évadé who reaches Georgetown or Port of Spain lands in American territory. Alternatively — the \"ugly exception\" — Washington takes it under a Havana-style trusteeship (Part A) after France defaults on its American debts. Noted, not settled."
