      "summary": "The KGC's northern successor, the Order of American Knights, re-formed in February 1864 as the Order of the Sons of Liberty (OSL), an oath-bound paramilitary society. Clement Vallandigham became its Supreme Commander around March 1864, while in exile. The OSL and Confederate commissioners in Canada worked toward a \"Northwestern Confederacy\" of Ohio, Indiana and Illinois. Chicago's OSL was estimated at \"about 2,000\" members by a contemporary account (another account says 4,000), under \"Brigadier-General\" Charles Walsh, with former mayor Buckner S. Morris as treasurer. The odd detail: a secret society with military ranks — a Chicago Copperhead held the title \"Brigadier-General\" of an army that existed only in its oath.",
