      "summary": "Grenfell, an English soldier of fortune who claimed to have fought in Algeria, Morocco, under Garibaldi in South America, in the Crimea and in the Indian Mutiny, rode with Morgan's Confederate cavalry and then joined the Chicago plot. Sentenced to hang by the Cincinnati commission, he had the sentence commuted to life by President Andrew Johnson through the efforts of the British Minister in Washington (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_St._Leger_Grenfell). At Fort Jefferson he was nursed through the September 1867 yellow-fever epidemic by fellow prisoner Dr. Samuel Mudd (the Lincoln-assassination conspirator). In March 1868 (Mudd's letter says the 6th; other sources the 7th) he and others escaped in a small open boat into a storm and were never seen again. In June 1868 the New York Times printed a report that a letter from him had arrived from Havana; historians generally treat it as fabrication. The odd detail: the last rumour of the Chicago conspirator puts him in Havana — the centre point of the Golden Circle's map.",
