      "summary": "Governor Oliver P. Morton learned from an informant that arms were being shipped from New York to Harrison H. Dodd, Indiana leader of the Sons of Liberty, who had pushed for an August rising to free the prisoners at Camp Morton. On August 20, 1864, troops raided his office and found 400 revolvers and thousands of rounds (one source: 135,000 (unverified — V_R10)) in boxes labelled \"Sunday school books\" (another source says \"Stationary\" (unverified — V_R10)). Dodd was tried by military commission, escaped jail and fled to Canada, and was sentenced to death in absentia (commuted to life, May 31, 1865). He later returned and settled in Fond du Lac, Wisconsin, where he served several terms as mayor — as a Republican — and died June 2, 1906. The odd detail: the Copperhead arsenal was shipped as Sunday-school books; its owner ended up a Republican mayor in Wisconsin.",
