      "summary": "The Camp Douglas dead were moved from the camp cemetery to Oak Woods and buried in concentric trenches — \"reputedly the largest documented mass grave in the Western Hemisphere.\" A monument and marker that former Kentucky lieutenant governor John C. Underwood helped build \"probably inflates\" the number buried as 6,000; the plaques list more than 4,000 names. The same cemetery holds Big Jim Colosimo (1920) and, later, Mayor William Hale Thompson (1944). The odd detail: the dead lie in rings — concentric trenches around a single monument — a literal circle of the Confederate dead in Chicago.",
