      "synopsis": "Original note includes uncertainty or estimates: Chicago drank raw lake water drawn through offshore intake cribs and tunnels 10–20 feet wide up to 200 feet beneath the lake bed. Keepers lived on the cribs (the Four-Mile had a heating plant from 1898 so men could winter there at 70°F; the 68th Street and Dunne cribs were joined by a footbridge so one crew served both).",
