      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — The owner already builds plots on real skies (the 1936 eclipse); the Elgin observatory is the one place in Illinois whose log records the sky every night to the second — a Section 13 analyst checks it for a missing minute. Elgin's State Hospital (R09) is across town; Sam Cowley died in Elgin's Sherman Hospital in 1934 (R02).",
