      "summary": "The Lake View Cemetery Association formed in July 1869 under Jeptha H. Wade and bought nearly 200 acres for $73,000; first lots were sold July 1870. The Garfield Monument (George H. Keller) opened on Memorial Day 1890; the Wade Memorial Chapel (1901) has a Tiffany interior. Buried here: President James A. Garfield, John D. Rockefeller (a trustee), Mark Hanna, Newton D. Baker, Charles F. Brush, Charles Chesnutt, and both Van Sweringen brothers (1935, 1936). There is a monument to the 169 pupils and 3 adults of the 1908 Collinwood School Fire, and a shared grave of the 19 children who could never be identified. It was a Sunday outing destination; by June 1891 it issued admission tickets. The odd detail: The cemetery's picturesque lakes were made by damming Dugway Creek — the dead of Cleveland's first families lie above water.",
