      "summary": "Built from 1871 (founded) / 1876 (opened — sources give both) to replace the old Espada Cemetery, designed by the Galician architect Calixto Arellano de Loira, who became its first occupant, dying before it was finished. Some 800,000 graves and over a million interments; a marble main gate (Faith, Hope and Charity) by José Vilalta Saavedra. The Monument to the Firefighters (sculptor Agustín Querol, architect Julio M. Zapata) honours the firemen killed in the hardware-store fire of 17 May 1890. Clara Maass (1901) and, legend has it, many of the Maine's dead lay here before removal; La Milagrosa is here; and in September 1932 the ABC tunnelled under its central avenue beside the Firefighters' Monument and laid dynamite (Part C). The odd detail: the architect as the first body in his own necropolis — and a secret society's tunnel under it thirty-six years later.",
