      "synopsis": "Oscar Merritt Wheelock, born 10 January 1877, a Somerville bookkeeper and auditor, was charged in January 1910 with misappropriating $9,200 from the Massachusetts Bonding and Insurance Co.; he fled to Butte, remarried (Winnie O'Malley), wrote a will on New Year's Eve 1910, and went to Mexico as Oscar G. Creighton in January 1911. Orozco and Villa, seeing him stand under fire at Bauche, gave him a captain's rank.",
