      "summary": "Founded in 1877 after Marie Silhanek, a Czech Catholic, was refused burial by several Catholic cemeteries for not making her Easter Duty; the Czech community bought its own ground. Mayor Anton Cermak, shot beside Roosevelt in Miami in February 1933 and dead March 6, lies in a mausoleum in Section 21. The cemetery holds Eastland victims (many of the dead were Czech Western Electric families) and is known for photograph-and-memento columbarium niches; in 2009 a Cubs fan built \"Beyond the Vines\", a Wrigley-wall columbarium with 288 niches and real stadium seats. The odd detail: The mayor of Chicago is buried in a cemetery that exists because the Church would not bury a woman.",
