      "summary": "The Weisz family arrived in the United States on 3 July 1878 aboard the SS Frisia and settled in Appleton, where the father, Rabbi Mayer Samuel Weisz, served the Zion Reform Jewish Congregation. In 1882 he lost the post and the family moved to Milwaukee. Houdini died on 31 October 1926 — Halloween — at Grace Hospital, Detroit, of peritonitis, after performing at the Garrick Theatre on 24 October with a 104°F fever, and a week after being punched in the abdomen. (R05, R13 and R32 carry the séance-debunker and Margery material; not repeated.) The odd detail: The man who is often said to have claimed Appleton as his birthplace (a commonly repeated claim; not on a page I read) had in fact arrived there in July 1878 as a small immigrant child (he was born in 1874, from memory) — and the family left because the rabbi lost his job.",
