      "title": "The Grand Kankakee Marsh",
      "date_start": "1882",
      "date_end": "1917",
      "date_label": "\"the Everglades of the North\", drained 1882–1917 (living memory)",
      "category": "Chicago's hinterland, 1925–1940: the collar counties, downstate Illinois and Northwest Indiana",
      "tags": [
        "Chicago",
        "hinterland",
        "Grand Kankakee Marsh",
        "living memory"
      ],
      "people": [
        "—"
      ],
      "places": [
        {
          "name": "The Kankakee River valley",
          "address": "",
          "geography": "NW Indiana and NE Illinois (~60 miles S/SE of Chicago): once 400,000 to over a million acres",
          "precision": "search locator, not surveyed",
          "map_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The%20Kankakee%20River%20valley%2C%20NW%20Indiana%20and%20NE%20Illinois%20%3A%20once%20400%2C000%20to%20over%20a%20million%20acres"
        },
        {
          "name": "English Lake and Beaver Lake",
          "address": "",
          "geography": "(Indiana's largest lake until the 1880s)",
          "precision": "search locator, not surveyed",
          "map_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=English%20Lake%20and%20Beaver%20Lake%2C%20Chicago"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "The river once ran 240 miles in more than 2,000 meander bends through a vast marsh that held over 225 bird species — flocks that could \"darken the sky\", passenger pigeons, cranes, eagles. Between 1882 and 1917 syndicates and the Indiana legislature straightened it into \"one of the largest drainage ditches in the U.S.\"; the loss has been put at one-fifth of America's migratory bird population, and Indiana lost 87% of its wetlands. The marsh had sheltered Native nations until the removal treaties (1821–36), and later the Underground Railroad and Black farming communities. The odd detail: A 1930s Chicagoan over 40 remembered a wilderness of water an hour south of the city that no longer existed — Beaver Lake, gone from the map.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
