      "summary": "Founded 1886 at Bishop Gilmour's invitation by Jesuits from Buffalo; a combined high school and college \"until 1902, when the latter assumed a separate existence.\" The college became Cleveland University and then John Carroll (1923) and left for University Heights in 1935 (R07, R05); the high school stayed on the old site, which it still occupies — it chose not to follow the city's Catholics to the suburbs. From 1971 it has been governed by a lay board rather than the Jesuits. The odd detail: For the whole decade the IHS seat (in the setting) had two addresses — a Gothic pile in the West Side immigrant district and a half-built tower in the Van Sweringens' suburb (R07's Fr. Odenbach lived in that tower in 1932–33).",
