      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the laws and dates (two scholarly summaries agree); Medium on peak population (6,078 from a search summary). • Laws followed: 31 March 1919 an 80%-Mexican-employees rule [and an order for separate \"Chinese neighbourhoods\" — UNVERIFIED — V_M08: the cited Szeged article puts the relocation order in 1923, and the 1923 laws are below];",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — a Sonoran Chinese laundryman or grocer who came for the copper towns; his tong and his temple; and a Sonoran-born mestizo child of a \"banned marriage.\" Report, don't villainise: the villains of this file are the leagues, not the Chinese. A Chicago Chinatown (Wentworth Avenue) cousin arrives at Nogales.",
