      "summary": "On 21 May 1891 the schooners Thomas Hume and Rouse Simmons left Chicago after unloading lumber; a squall hit; the Rouse Simmons turned back, the Hume \"continued on, and disappeared\" with six men. (Found intact in 150 ft of water only in 2006; judged a storm loss.) In October 1921 the schooner Rosabelle, which carried materials for the House of David religious colony at Benton Harbor, sailed with potatoes and maple lumber; her captain refused to board, saying he had a premonition of disaster; she was found capsized, stern missing as if in a collision, no crew aboard — yet no ship reported a collision and the Coast Guard concluded there had been none. The odd detail: The Rosabelle belonged to a millenarian sect (R05 covers the House of David) and its captain stayed ashore on a premonition.",
