      "import_supplement": true,
      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "The Great Northern Railway built four ore docks at Allouez Bay — Dock One in 1892, Two in 1899–1900, Three in 1902–03, Four in 1911 — the largest gravity iron-ore dock installation in the world. The Northern Pacific built a concrete-and-steel dock in 1913 on the west bank of the Nemadji, designed to handle high-grade Cuyuna ore, expanded in 1917 and 1925 to a final length of 1,860 feet.",
