      "id": "R30-016",
      "title": "Chicago Harbor Light — the fair's lighthouse, moved out to the breakwater",
      "date_start": "1893",
      "date_end": "1919",
      "date_label": "1893 / 1919 / all decade",
      "category": "The lakes themselves, 1925–1940: ships, sailors, wrecks, storms, lighthouses, the Coast Guard, smugglers and the lake economy",
