      "summary": "The fair's official timeline records German Day on Thursday, 15 June 1893, one of the great national days of the fair. Imperial Germany built its own German Government Building (photographed by William Henry Jackson), with the Germania Fountain — Germania on a globe holding a lamp aloft — as part of the German showing; Wikipedia notes the German Building was among the few structures that \"remained standing after the Expo.\" Together with the Krupp pavilion and the Midway village this made Germany the most conspicuous foreign presence of 1893. The odd detail: The German Building outlived the White City (UNVERIFIED how long — see leads).",
