      "id": "R15-015",
      "title": "Poles against the Pope — Kozłowski's schism, \"Bishop\" Vilatte, and the Polish National Catholic Church",
      "date_start": "1895",
      "date_end": "1929",
      "date_label": "1895 to 1929+",
      "category": "Immigrant and Ethnic Chicago in the 1930s",
      "tags": [
        "ethnic Chicago",
        "immigrants",
        "Poles",
        "Pope",
        "Kozłowski's"
      ],
      "people": [
        "Anthony Kozłowski",
        "Joseph René Vilatte",
        "Stanislaus Segers",
        "Andrew Kwasigroch"
      ],
      "places": [
        {
          "name": "All Saints independent church",
          "address": "",
          "geography": "St. Hedwig's parish district (Bucktown/Avondale)",
          "precision": "search locator, not surveyed",
          "map_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=All%20Saints%20independent%20church%2C%20St.%20Hedwig%27s%20parish%20district%2C%20Chicago"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "On 11 Aug 1895 the followers of ex-priest Anthony Kozłowski hung banners — \"Welcome Your Eminence, the Bishop, For Coming to Bless the Church of All Saints\" — but the \"bishop\" did not come; Kozłowski blessed the church himself. The Catholic Dziennik Chicagoski sneered that \"his eminence\" was \"a cook from Green Bay by the name of Vilatte,\" and noted a Muslim crescent flag and a \"Muscovite\" flag among the decorations. Rumours claimed a telegram from the Pope or a bishop \"from Cleveland.\" The same year a Polish anti-clerical sheet, Djabeł (\"The Devil,\" renamed Kropidło, \"The Holy-Water Sprinkler\"), printed that St. Stanislaus Kostka's organist Andrew Kwasigroch had murdered his maid and been shielded by Fr. Barzynski; publisher Stanislaus Segers was convicted of criminal libel (Nov 1895). By 1929 the independent movement's paper Przebudzenie (\"Awakening\") was arguing that the \"papal church\" had never protested Poland's partition and had condemned the 1831 rising, and that \"the only 'National' Church for Poles … is the Polish National Catholic Church.\" The odd detail: a Polish church consecrated without a bishop, under a crescent flag, awaiting a wandering \"archbishop\" from Wisconsin (Joseph René Vilatte, an Old Catholic episcopus vagans).",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High for what the papers printed; Vilatte's full identification is the paper's and general knowledge — Medium.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — \"no one is clean\" inside the Church: a schismatic Polish church outside IHS's reach, ordained by a wandering bishop whose line of succession is irregular — exactly where a Kabbalah or a cult could buy a consecration IHS can't police.",
