      "synopsis": "On 11 Aug 1895 the followers of ex-priest Anthony Kozłowski hung banners — \"Welcome Your Eminence, the Bishop, For Coming to Bless the Church of All Saints\" — but the \"bishop\" did not come; Kozłowski blessed the church himself. The Catholic Dziennik Chicagoski sneered that \"his eminence\" was \"a cook from Green Bay by the name of Vilatte,\" and noted a Muslim crescent flag and a \"Muscovite\" flag among the decorations.",
