      "summary": "Fr. Wilhelm Grutza bought 200,000 tons of stone from Chicago's demolished U.S. Custom House, Court House and Post Office for $20,000 and moved it north on 500 railroad flatcars; architect Erhard Brielmaier redesigned his brick church around the salvage, including the old building's granite columns and carved capitals. Completed 1901 in the \"Polish cathedral\" style under a 214-ft dome; Tadeusz Żukotyński painted the first mural (1904); stained glass came from Austria (1902). In 1929 Pius XI made it the third minor basilica in the United States. An electrical fire in 1940 caused smoke damage. The odd detail: Milwaukee's Poles worship inside the carcass of Chicago's old federal courthouse and post office.",
