      "summary": "Born in Munich May 15, 1896, Kuhn won the Iron Cross as a German infantry lieutenant in the Great War, moved to Mexico in the 1920s, and came to the U.S. in 1928, working at a Ford factory in Detroit; he was naturalised in 1934. He took control of the Bund at Buffalo in 1936, led 50 followers to the Berlin Olympics, and claimed afterward that Hitler had recognised him as \"American Führer\" (the meeting had in fact disappointed him). Convicted December 5, 1939 of embezzling $14,548 from the Bund — part of it spent on a mistress — he went to Sing Sing the next day. The odd detail: America's would-be Führer learned the country on Ford's Detroit assembly line after a stint in Mexico.",
