      "divergence": "BENDS HARD — America never entered the Great War, so the 370th never went to France. The Eighth Illinois's real prior service was on the Mexican border in 1916 (from memory — the regiment was called up for the Punitive Expedition period; UNVERIFIED this session), and in the setting that is where its war is: the Southern War of 1916–17 and the occupation after it. The 137 names on the shaft at 35th and South Parkway died at Tampico, Veracruz or in the mineral north; the battle names on the tablet are Mexican; the \"victory\" is the one over Mexico. The regiment is a garrison of the empire — and Black Chicago's relationship to a colonial war fought against another non-white people is a live moral wound for a module. Rulebook note: this is the setting's own \"Great War story\" for Black Chicago.",
