      "summary": "Indiana had no waiting period for a marriage licence, so couples from Chicago eloped to Crown Point and married the same day; the town was called the \"Marriage Mill\". Among those married there: Rudolph Valentino and Tom Mix (later, Muhammad Ali and Joseph Jackson). The famous claim that Ronald Reagan and Jane Wyman married there is false (Glendale, California). On 3 March 1934 Dillinger walked out of the county jail with a wooden gun and took Sheriff Lillian Holley's new V-8 Ford (R02). The odd detail: The same county seat processed Hollywood elopements and Dillinger's escape — a courthouse where people went to bind themselves quickly and a jail no one could hold.",
