      "summary": "The Temple of Music — Italian Renaissance, 180-ft dome, 2,000 seats, $85,000, painted light yellow with gold and red and a light-blue dome, with a 52-rank pipe organ — was where President William McKinley greeted the public on 6 September 1901 and was shot by the anarchist Leon Czolgosz; McKinley died in Buffalo a week later. All the fair buildings were demolished; the exact spot of the shooting has been argued over for a century. The odd detail: Nobody is sure exactly where the President was standing — the marker is a best guess.",
