      "summary": "Benjamin and Mary Purnell founded the House of David in 1903 as Christian Israelites claiming succession from the English prophetess Joanna Southcott; members were celibate, vegetarian and teetotal, did not cut their hair and did not handle the dead, and aimed to gather the 144,000 Israelites to be made immortal at Christ's return. They reached about 1,000 members by 1916 and ran a 125-acre amusement park with a zoo and miniature trains, touring bands, and famous barnstorming baseball teams of bearded players (Satchel Paige played for them). Benjamin was arrested in 1926 on statutory-rape charges — the trial produced over 15,000 pages of testimony — and died in December 1927. In 1930 the colony split: Mary led Mary's City of David, while Benjamin's successor Judge H. T. Dewhirst led the House of David. The odd detail: A celibate immortality cult that was best known to the public for its long-haired baseball team and an amusement park.",
