      "summary": "Stanley Robert McCormick (1874–1947), youngest son of the reaper inventor, married the MIT-trained Katharine Dexter on September 15, 1904. He was already \"showing signs of progressively worsening mental illness\"; in September 1906 he went into McLean Hospital with dementia praecox (schizophrenia), and from June 1908 he was kept at Riven Rock under the care of Emil Kraepelin's methods. In 1909 he was declared legally incompetent and \"his guardianship divided between Katharine and the McCormick family\" — the start of decades of litigation between the wife and the Chicago McCormicks over who controlled him and his money (the 1929–30 Santa Barbara court fight is remembered but UNVERIFIED this session). He died January 19, 1947, aged 72, leaving Katharine over $35 million, 85 per cent of which went in taxes; she spent $2 million of the rest developing the contraceptive pill. The odd detail: One of the richest men in America spent the whole decade a prisoner in his own estate, his person the subject of a lawsuit between his wife and his brothers.",
