          "marker": "V_M03 — the two condemned in the Zoila case were Bocourt and Víctor Molina (accused of doing the killing and taking the heart); both were executed by garrote in 1906, the first and only executions among the 24 \"ritual crime\" cases the period press ran between 1904 and 1924 (Aisthesis 46). Aisthesis also says Bocourt and other cabildo members were first arrested and released for lack of evidence, then re-arrested when the child's body turned up, and that the press claim that Bocourt had \"salted\" the body was contradicted by the expert examinations.",
