      "summary": "In 1905 Norwegian men from Chicago founded the Norge Ski Club here and built ski jumps — it is called the oldest continuously open ski club in the US. Eman Opatrny's Picnic Grove (1899: picnic plots, a shooting gallery, a horse track, six bars, a boathouse) burned in 1918. Louis Cernocky Sr. built the eight-sided Crystal Ballroom at \"Louie's Place\" in 1923 — Glenn Miller and Guy Lombardo played it, and members of the Dillinger and Barker-Karpis gangs were regulars (R02 has the gang side). In 1939 a strange incident — arson, kerosene-soaked floors, a kidnapping and planted bombs — hit the Crystal Ballroom, and it never reopened for dancing. The odd detail: Ski-jumpers in the air over the Fox River in winter; gangsters at the ballroom bar in summer; and in 1939 the ballroom is soaked in kerosene and bombed.",
