      "summary": "Golda Mabovitch arrived in Milwaukee in 1906 when her father found work in the railroad shops, was valedictorian at Fourth Street School (1906–12) despite absences for work, went to North Division High (1912) while clerking at Schuster's and the public library, ran away to Denver and came back, entered the State Normal School in 1916, joined Young Poale Zion and spoke for socialist Zionism on Milwaukee street corners, taught at a Yiddish folk school in 1917, and on 24 December 1917 married Morris Meyerson, sign-painter, on condition they go to Palestine — which they did in 1921 on the SS Pocahontas. The odd detail: The future prime minister of Israel was a Milwaukee library clerk who preached Zionism on Walnut Street.",
