      "summary": "Legend makes Jesús Malverde (b. \"1870\") a Robin Hood bandit under Governor Francisco Cañedo, hanged on 3 May 1909 and left unburied to rot — people threw stones on the spot until a cairn rose, then a chapel. His existence is not historically verified; Sam Quinones suggests he fuses the real bandits Heraclio Bernal (1855–1888) and Felipe Bachomo (1883–1916). The chapel dates from the 1970s; his association with drug traffickers is later still. The odd detail: a saint's shrine that began as a pile of stones thrown on an unburied body.",
