      "summary": "Zemurray's Cuyamel Fruit Company stood to lose if Honduras's President Dávila enforced debt terms tied to a U.S. bank loan; Secretary of State Philander Knox rejected his appeals. So he bought a ship (the Hornet), had Lee Christmas recruit about 100 mercenaries in New Orleans (Sam Dreben among them), and chose the man to install: Bonilla. His reward was \"very favorable tax and land concessions\" (Wikipedia). Decades later, as president of United Fruit, he authorised Edward Bernays's campaign against Guatemala's Jacobo Árbenz, and the CIA coup of 1954 followed. The odd detail: one man bought the ship, the army and the president — and forty-odd years later did it again with a public-relations man instead of a mercenary.",
