      "summary": "When Maderista forces took Torreón, 308 Asians — 303 Chinese and 5 Japanese — were killed, nearly half of the city's Chinese population, by revolutionary troops (under Emilio Madero) together with mobs from surrounding towns and local residents. Local revolutionary Jesús Flores incited it with speeches claiming the Chinese monopolised the grocery trade and \"put Mexican women out of jobs\" and demanding their expulsion. Chinese community leaders had circulated warnings on 12 May for people to hide. Property damage came to about $1 million, of which $849,928.69 was Chinese property. The Qing government first demanded 30 million pesos, later reduced to 6 million; a 1912 treaty awarded 3.1 million pesos, which was never paid. An investigation called it \"an unprovoked massacre … conceived in malice and race hatred.\" President López Obrador apologised in 2021. The odd detail: the massacre was announced in advance by the victims' own leaders, who told everyone to hide — and the killers were the revolution's \"democratic\" side; the debt outlived the president who signed it.",
