      "summary": "From around 1915 the Ku Klux Klan circulated a forged \"Fourth Degree oath\" in which Knights of Columbus supposedly swore to exterminate Freemasons and Protestants. The Knights called it libel and sued distributors; in 1914 they set up lectures and educational programs against anti-Catholic propaganda, and in 1923 offered $25,000 to anyone who could prove the oath was part of any real ceremony. The Klan eventually stopped printing it. The odd detail: a forged oath was used to recruit for a real one — the Klan's own oath.",
