      "summary": "A Serbian school opened in 1912 at 14th and Massachusetts, with Paul Veljkov as its first teacher (he later became the parish's second priest). The parish of Saint Sava was formed on 15 February 1914 and incorporated 16 April 1914; its first church was consecrated 13 June 1915. In the 1920s internal division became a schism: a rival parish, Holy Resurrection, was set up at 39th and Washington in Glen Park; the congregations reunified by the late 1930s, laid a cornerstone in 1937, and consecrated the new church on 24 November 1938. By the late 1950s it was the largest Eastern Orthodox parish in Gary. (The 1938–39 building burned on 16 February 1978.) The odd detail: A Serbian Orthodox schism in a steel town in the 1920s — over the church's canonical control, with the rivalry so bitter it split a small parish into two.",
