      "summary": "On 14 October 1912 at 8:10 p.m. John Schrank (a New York saloonkeeper, from memory) shot Roosevelt in the chest outside the Gilpatrick Hotel; the bullet passed through Roosevelt's folded 50-page speech and eyeglass case and broke a rib, and Roosevelt gave a 50-minute speech before seeing a doctor. Schrank said that on 15 September 1901 — the day after McKinley died — McKinley's body rose from its coffin, said \"Avenge my death!\" and pointed at Roosevelt; and that on 14 September 1912 the dead president's apparition, \"with dying eyes,\" commanded him to stop Roosevelt's third term. Judge August C. Backus refused his guilty plea, a sanity commission found him insane on 22 November 1912, and he was committed with \"dementia praecox, paranoid type.\" He died on 15 September 1943, after 31 years in Wisconsin's asylums, reportedly without a visitor or letter. (The Wikipedia page on Schrank places the first commitment \"in Waupun\"; the Winnebago hospital's page says Oshkosh — the two disagree; Waupun is where he died. The commitment order quoted on the Schrank page itself names the Northern Hospital for the Insane \"near Oshkosh\" (22 Nov 1912), so Oshkosh came first.) The odd detail: He died on 15 September, the same calendar day as his first ghost dream, forty-two years later.",
