      "synopsis": "Original note includes uncertainty or estimates: Captain Herman Schuenemann and his brother August had been selling Christmas trees off schooners at Chicago since the 1890s; August had already died when the S. Thal sank in a November 1898 storm. On 23 Nov 1912 the three-masted Rouse Simmons foundered in a gale bound for the Clark Street dock with about 5,500 trees; all 17 aboard died.",
