      "summary": "Leopoldo Ruiz y Flores, Archbishop of Morelia (Michoacán) from 1911, fled the Constitutionalists in 1914; the DHIAL entry says he \"tuvo que irse a vivir a la ciudad de Chicago\" (\"had to go and live in the city of Chicago\") — making him the most senior Mexican prelate to live in Chicago in the first exile. Expelled again by Calles in 1927, he returned to the US; as apostolic delegate he co-signed the arreglos of 21 June 1929; expelled a third time in October 1932 (see Part B), he lived in San Antonio until 1938. He died on 12 December 1941 — the feast of Our Lady of Guadalupe. The odd detail: the man who ended the Cristero War had once been a refugee in Chicago, a decade before Chicago had a Mexican parish.",
