      "import_supplement": false,
      "collection": "Mexico & Caribbean",
      "synopsis": "On 15 March 1914 the bowsman Simplício and Kermit were in a dugout in the rapids; a whirlpool tore them into mid-stream, the boat filled and overturned, and Roosevelt wrote: \"Poor Simplicio must have been pulled under at once\". Kermit clung to the overturned boat, was swept downstream and reached an overhanging branch and shore with his dog Trigueiro (the dog's name is in Roosevelt's text), almost drowned.",
