      "summary": "The new light cruiser Karlsruhe left Kiel on 14 June 1914 and reached St Thomas on 1 July. On 6 August, about 120 nautical miles north of Watling Island, she met the North German Lloyd liner Kronprinz Wilhelm to arm her as a raider — only two 8.8 cm guns, a machine gun and some sailors had crossed when HMS Suffolk appeared; she outran Suffolk and Bristol and reached Puerto Rico on 9 August almost out of coal. Off northeast Brazil she took or sank sixteen merchantmen (fifteen British, one Dutch; 72,805 GRT). On 4 November 1914, about 18:30, steaming for a raid on Barbados, she was torn apart by a spontaneous internal explosion; ~146 survivors reached her colliers Rio Negro and Indrani. Berlin hid the loss; the Royal Navy kept hunting her until March 1915. The odd detail: for four months the British Caribbean was guarding against a ship that was already at the bottom of the sea.",
