      "summary": "Captain Franz von Papen, military attaché accredited to both Washington and Mexico, was in Mexico in July 1914, \"observing, among other matters, the effect of dynamite explosions on railways\", according to the 1918 account; he \"organized a military unit in the lukewarm German colony in Mexico City\" and \"used one or more of the warring factions in the southern republic to test the efficacy of various means of warfare.\" The same book gives the doctrine in one line: \"Mexico must divert America's attention from Europe and remove to the border her available forces.\" Papen was declared persona non grata and left the United States in December 1915 (declared persona non grata on 3 December 1915). The odd detail: the future Chancellor of Germany (in our 1932) learned his trade watching Mexican trains blow up.",
