      "summary": "The Chicago sausage maker Oscar Mayer went hunting in north-eastern Canada six weeks into the war with Mayor Carter Harrison Jr. and Joseph Winter. The guides had been told the party was French-Canadian. \"When Oscar Mayer, after a missing shot, began to swear in the German language,\" the guides reported the party as German spies and Mayer was arrested; the Staats-Zeitung, in its coverage of the autumn election campaign, said the news \"was treated in the beginning as a joke\" but \"has been confirmed as a fact\", adding that Judge Cooper \"has been very sympathetic with the affairs of the Germans.\" The odd detail: the mayor of Chicago was in the Canadian woods with a German sausage manufacturer in September 1914, and it was the sausage man they arrested.",
