      "summary": "The American troops had occupied the lighthouse building in 1914. When they left, Venustiano Carranza moved his Constitutionalist government in, declaring Veracruz the capital of the nation until October 1915, while Villa and Zapata held Mexico City. From the lighthouse came the Agrarian Law of 6 January 1915 — the foundation of Mexican land reform — and the Law of Free Municipalities. Carranza also closed the prison of San Juan de Ulúa (next entry). The odd detail: modern Mexico's land reform was written in a lighthouse the US Army had just vacated, paid for by a port whose customs money the Americans had just carried off.",
