      "summary": "Mayor William Hale Thompson earned the nickname \"Kaiser Bill\" for opposing US entry into the war, declining to host the French mission and allowing anti-war meetings; he was \"credited with characterizing Chicago as the sixth German city of the world.\" In his 1927 comeback he promised Irish voters he would punch King George V \"in the nose\" (or arrest him), called the King \"the biggest enemy the United States had,\" and moved against Superintendent William McAndrew for pro-British textbooks (the board charged McAndrew with \"insubordination and lack of patriotism,\" Aug 1927). Capone gave over $200,000 to the 1927 campaign and ~$260,000 in 1931. In 1931 he called Cermak a \"Bohunk\" and sang \"Tony, Tony, where's your pushcart at?\"; Cermak answered, \"it's true I didn't come over on the Mayflower, but I came over as soon as I could,\" and won with 58%. The odd detail: Chicago's mayor ran against a foreign king — and, in 1931, lost to an immigrant by mocking immigrants in the most immigrant city in America.",
