      "summary": "Bennett, Henry Ford's closest man, built the Ford Service Department out of football players, boxers, wrestlers and Detroit River gang members, and used it for spying on and beating union men through the 1930s (he denied involvement in the Overpass beating despite witnesses). He was Ford's enforcer from 1915 until Henry Ford II pushed him out in 1945. The odd detail: His Huron River estate held pet lions and tigers and hidden passageways; his Farwell lodge had a secret passage to the dock behind a hinged bookcase, an underwater pool-viewing room with a wet bar, and a moat full of pointed posts crossed by a bridge wired with dynamite.",
