      "summary": "\"Several hundred\" of the 844 Eastland dead were Czech-Americans. Denní Hlasatel (1 Aug 1915) printed photographs of the funeral of the whole Novotný family — Václav and Anežka, daughter Marie and little Vilík — with Boy Scouts, schoolchildren and Sokol youth marching down 26th St., watched by thousands; Mayor Thompson attended. Cicero was \"mourning\"; a Czech relief committee (Český Vypomocný Výbor) formed and disbanded within seven weeks (unverified — V_R15). The odd detail: a whole family buried from a freethought school — secular Czech Chicago's own funeral rite.",
