      "summary": "Major Smedley Butler, with about 100 Marines and sailors, attacked the last caco stronghold of the First Caco War. The Marines found a partially sealed drain four feet wide, three feet high and fifteen feet deep in the wall; Sgt. Ross Lindsey Iams and Pvt. Samuel Gross crawled through first, Butler behind them with his pistol. More than 50 cacos were killed, including their commander Josaphat Jean-Joseph; no Marine was killed (one lost two teeth to a thrown rock). All three men received the Medal of Honor — Butler's second. The Marines then dynamited the fort and destroyed some 60 dwellings around it. The odd detail: Butler's own verdict — the defenders \"could have shot us like rats\" as they came out of the hole.",
