      "summary": "Camp Wilson became the Texas Guard's mobilisation point in May 1916 and then the tent city of the Guard brigades around San Antonio, where the Illinois regiments were sent (the Illinois camp is reported \"near San Antonio\"; its exact site is not confirmed this session). In mid-September 14,000 Guardsmen from Illinois, Wisconsin, Kansas, Texas and Missouri made a fifteen-day, 166-mile practice march from San Antonio toward New Braunfels and back. Over November–December the 12th Provisional Division ran a football tournament: on Christmas Day 1916 the 3rd Illinois lost the championship to the 1st Wisconsin, 9–0. The odd detail: the German Hill Country — New Braunfels, Fredericksburg, Comfort — was where the march went: Illinois boys hiking through Texas towns where the shop signs and church services were in German, in the summer America was deciding whose side it was on.",
