      "summary": "Milton Hershey first visited Cuba in January 1916, bought the Central San Juan Bautista and built Central Hershey, a sugar mill finished in 1918, with a model batey (mill town) on the pattern of Hershey, Pennsylvania: rented houses, a clinic, a baseball diamond, golf course and club, a general store and free schooling. To move the sugar he built an all-electric railway between Havana and Matanzas, completed in October 1922. He bought more mills in 1920, 1925 and 1927. The first pupils of his Hershey Agricultural School were boys orphaned by a 1923 wreck on the Hershey Cuban railroad. Sold in 1946: 60,000 acres, 5 mills, 4 power plants, 251 miles of track. The odd detail: an orphan school founded for the children whose parents the company's own train had killed.",
