      "collection": "Mexico & Caribbean",
      "synopsis": "The 7th Illinois Infantry, raised from the Hibernian Rifles (a Chicago Irish civilian-military society), was mustered into federal service on 27 June 1916 and did not muster out until 26 January 1917 — three and a half months after the 1st Illinois went home. The Argus of 30 June recorded the Seventh being put on the train for \"San Anton\".",
