      "title": "What the wards did to patients in the 1930s: fever, insulin, Metrazol, the continuous tub",
      "date_start": "1917",
      "date_end": "1941",
      "date_label": "Illinois practice, 1917–1941",
      "category": "Places of confinement in Chicago and Illinois, 1925–1940",
