      "divergence": "BENDS — major. In the setting February 1917 is the war's end and the treaty's season. A constitution declaring the subsoil national, written while Americans hold the oil and mineral north, is either (a) the defiant charter of a defeated rump Mexico — Article 27 as an unenforceable claim on the ceded north's minerals and Tampico's oil — or (b) never written in this form. Recommend (a): it gives Mexico a legal grievance the treaty cannot extinguish. Article 130 then applies only in UNCEDED MEXICO — the ceded north, under American law, keeps its churches open: the Cristero War becomes a war the American border does not cross.",
