      "divergence": "THE HINGE — BENDS. The February 1917 landing happens (pre-dates the April declaration). Then: Cuba does not declare war on Germany — ALTERNATE_HISTORY §30.7 already rules Cuba and Panama stay neutral because they followed America in, and America never goes in. So the occupation's real cover story (a wartime ally's harvest) disappears; the Marines stay in Oriente on the naked sugar-and-order pretext — and never leave (§8.2). The August 1917 reinforcement, sent in the record for the war, needs another reason in the setting: the Southern War next door is the obvious one.",
