      "summary": "In Denmark a non-binding referendum on 14 December 1916 favoured the sale (283,670 for; 158,157 against); the Danish parliament ratified the treaty on 22 December. At 4:00 pm on 31 March 1917, as the Danish flag came down and the American flag went up over Charlotte Amalie in a somber, silent ceremony, a warrant for $25 million was handed in Washington to the Danish minister, Constantin Brun (the National Museum of Denmark says the sum was paid \"in gold coin\"). The islands — St. Thomas, St. John and St. Croix — were then governed by the U.S. Navy. The odd detail: the ceremony was two ceremonies at once, one in the Caribbean and one in an office in Washington, timed to the same afternoon.",
