      "summary": "The Black population rose from about 6,000 (1910) to 20,000 (1917) as migrants came for industrial jobs; when the Aluminum Ore Company hired Black strikebreakers, a 28 May labour meeting heard rumours of \"Black men fraternizing with white women\", and violence began. On 1 July white men fired into a Black neighbourhood; residents then fired on a second car — which carried police, killing a detective. Next day crowds came to see the bloodstained car, then rushed the Black districts. Congress's investigators counted at least 39 Black and 8 white dead (estimates run to 150); 6,000 were driven from their homes. On 28 July about 10,000 people walked in the Silent Parade down Fifth Avenue in New York. The odd detail: The massacre was triggered by the exhibition of a bullet-riddled police car to a crowd.",
