      "summary": "Mother Cabrini, naturalised American (1909), founded 67 institutions, including two Chicago hospitals. On 21 Dec 1917 she wrapped Christmas sweets for the children of her school; she died unexpectedly at about 1 p.m. on Saturday 22 Dec in her private room at Columbus Hospital. Mundelein — the last outsider she spoke to (unverified — V_R05) — said her funeral Mass in the hospital chapel; her body lay in state in Chicago and New York and was buried at West Park, NY. Exhumed during the cause in 1933, her body had decayed normally except for the skeleton and a heart \"still fleshy\"; relics were divided — skull to Rome, heart to Codogno, the trunk in a wax effigy in New York; her arm bone (humerus) is now in the Chicago shrine. Pius XI beatified her on 13 Nov 1938 (miracles: the blind boy Peter Smith in New York, Sr. Delphina Grazioli in Seattle). Canonised 1946, first American citizen saint. The odd detail: She died on 22 December — solstice day, the date of the setting's alpha adventure — after spending her last evening wrapping Christmas candy.",
