      "divergence": "BENDS — CEDED NORTH. In the setting Ciudad Juárez is American after 1917, so the whole rationale of a foreign bar-town beside a dry Texas disappears: Juárez is a dry American city too (Prohibition holds domestically). Two setting fixes: (a) the cantinas persist as an occupation-era exemption (the occupier keeps its troops' liquor in the \"Zone\"), or (b) the drinking town moves to the Tamaulipas reach (Nuevo Laredo, Matamoros) — see the tequileros entry. The \"Chicago\" link (Capone at the Kentucky Bar) is a legend; if the owner likes it, it can be made true.",
