      "summary": "Born at a normal 8 lb 5 oz, Robert Pershing Wadlow outgrew his father (5 ft 11½) by age 8; a pituitary disorder was diagnosed at 12 and his parents refused risky surgery. At his 1936 high-school graduation he was 8 ft 4 in; that year he toured with Ringling Brothers at Madison Square Garden and Boston Garden, insisting on everyday clothes, never a costume; from 1938 he toured for the International Shoe Company, which gave him his shoes free. A faulty leg brace raised a blister on 4 July 1940; the infection killed him in his sleep on 15 July at Manistee, aged 22. Final measured height 8 ft 11.1 in (27 June 1940). His coffin was 10 ft 9 in long and needed 12 pallbearers and 8 assistants. The odd detail: The tallest man in recorded history was a polite young man from a river town who would not wear a circus costume — and he was touring the Midwest through the whole setting decade.",
