      "summary": "Congress authorised the Mexican Border Service Medal on 9 July 1918 for service on the border between 9 May 1916 and 24 March 1917 (or from 1 January 1916 to 6 April 1917 for troops assigned to the border patrol). It was for service inside the United States; men who crossed into Mexico or fought there got the separate Mexican Service Medal instead, and no one could have both. The ribbon: emerald green, golden yellow, emerald green. The odd detail: the medal is a class marker — a green-yellow-green ribbon tells another veteran at a glance whether you stood on the Texas side or went in.",
