      "unverified": [],
      "divergence": "BENDS hard — CEDED NORTH. In the setting Sonora is American by 1917 and the year 1918 is not a Great War year for the U.S., so the German-agent rumour is not about the U.S. war effort but about Germany as patron of other people's revolutions. There is no international line at Nogales — the two towns are one American city and the \"fence\" of 1918 is at best a military cordon. Notably the source of the fence (the Sonoran governor agreeing) would have to be an American military governor.",
