      "summary": "Before Prohibition Peoria had more distilleries than any other US city — over 24 distilleries and 73 breweries between 1837 and 1919 — and paid huge federal liquor tax. Under Prohibition it became \"one of the major bootlegging areas\" and the base of the Shelton Brothers Gang (after their war with Birger, Part G). Caterpillar Tractor was formed there in 1925 (Holt + Best). \"Will it play in Peoria?\" is vaudeville slang of uncertain origin, often wrongly credited to Groucho Marx. The odd detail: The river town that made America's whiskey became the headquarters of the gang that had bombed a roadhouse from an aeroplane.",
