      "divergence": "BENDS, sharply. Prohibition holds (domestic calendar; repeal Dec 1933). But if the Bahamas are American, Nassau cannot be the legal warehouse — American law would run there. So the rum trade itself is an argument for §8.6: either the Bahamas stay British through the 1920s (and Nassau's boom happens as recorded, with an American lease elsewhere in the islands), or the Americans buy them and the whisky moves to the next foreign port — Havana under occupation, Saint-Pierre, Belize, Curaçao.",
