      "summary": "Goodyear's Type FD dirigible Wingfoot Air Express was carrying passengers between Grant Park and the White City amusement park when, at about 4:55 p.m., its hydrogen caught fire for unknown reasons. It fell onto the Illinois Trust and Savings building and flaming debris crashed through the skylight into the banking hall. Thirteen died — three crew and passengers and ten bank employees. Pilot Jack Boettner parachuted to safety; a mechanic's parachute caught fire, and another man hung fifty feet below the burning gondola on tangled lines. It was the worst airship accident in the US to that date; Chicago wrote new aviation rules and built the Chicago Air Park, later Midway Airport. The odd detail: An airship from Akron fell into a bank in Chicago's financial district — the ten dead were clerks at their desks.",
