      "summary": "Wikipedia's Torso article: \"Most victims came from an area east of Kingsbury Run called 'The Roaring Third' or 'Hobo Jungle', known for its bars, gambling dens, brothels and vagrants.\" In late 1935 Ness abolished the precinct system altogether and reorganised the city into police districts, each under a captain (later five districts in 32 zones, with radio zone cars around the clock replacing foot patrolmen). The department had 1,384 officers in 1921 and fitted its first radio transmitter and car receivers in 1929. The odd detail: \"The Roaring Third\" stopped existing on paper the year the murders started — Ness redrew the police map in December 1935, three months after the first two bodies at Jackass Hill.",
