      "summary": "Facing the Sonorans' Plan of Agua Prieta (23 April 1920 — Obregón, Calles, de la Huerta), President Venustiano Carranza left Mexico City on 7 May 1920 with the \"Column of Legality\" — a railway convoy carrying the National Treasury — for Veracruz. At Aljibes he learned the line was cut and Veracruz lost. Going on by horse into the Puebla sierra, his party accepted an escort from Gen. Rodolfo Herrero, who led them to Tlaxcalantongo, excused himself to see a wounded brother, and returned before dawn with men who shot into Carranza's hut at 4:30 a.m. [time UNVERIFIED — V_M01; Wikipedia lists the cause of death as \"assassination (possibly suicide)\" — Herrero later said Carranza, wounded in the leg, shot himself, citing eyewitnesses; murder is the usual account, not the only one] The odd detail: a president fleeing on a train made of the national treasury toward the one port the Americans had just given back — and dying in a hut in the rain.",
