      "summary": "On 31 May 1920 a group of Black youths threw rocks at cars on Sheridan Road and broke the windshield of a car belonging to a naval officer's wife (\"U.S. Navy Lieutenant Mrs. Blazler,\" per the source). Sailors and Marines from the Great Lakes Naval Training Station then gathered — hundreds, shouting \"Lynch 'em!\" — outside the Sherman House, smashed windows, overturned furniture and attacked Black residents. The Chicago-gang-history page adds that Waukegan's chief of police and State's Attorney were members of the Ku Klux Klan. The odd detail: The rioters came from the Great Lakes Naval Training Station just south of Waukegan — the same station whose closing (1933) and reopening (1935) R29 tells.",
