      "summary": "Wanderer, a veteran who claimed to be heavily decorated (comrades later doubted it), told police a ragged robber had shot his pregnant wife Ruth in their vestibule and that he had shot the robber dead. Ben Hecht (Daily News) noticed the \"penniless drifter\" carried a Colt .45 identical to Wanderer's; Charles MacArthur (Examiner) traced it to Wanderer's cousin; Sgt. John Norton found the 17-year-old stenographer. Wanderer had hired the stranger for a staged fight and shot them both. He got 25 years for Ruth and death for the stranger — whose name was never fixed (John Maloney, Al Watson, John Barrett...) until a woman claimed him in Aug 1921 as a son she had given to a farmer eighteen years before. Wanderer sang \"Old Pal, Why Don't You Answer Me\" on the gallows. The odd detail: The man he was hanged for killing had no certain name; the murderer sang.",
