      "summary": "In 1921 Pershing chose him as an honorary pallbearer at the burial of the Unknown Soldier at Arlington (the article lists him with Alvin York). That same year he took part in an illegal attempt to extradite an escaped prisoner, Phil Alguin, from Ciudad Juárez, using a fake medical office; everyone involved was arrested and released after three days under U.S. pressure. After divorcing Helen Spence he ran a successful insurance business in El Paso; in 1923 he married Meade Andrews and moved to California. On 15 March 1925 he died in Los Angeles when, the article says, a nurse accidentally injected him with the wrong substance. The New York Times and El Paso Times ran obituaries; Damon Runyon wrote a eulogy; the Texas Legislature adjourned for a day in his honour; he is buried at Grand View Memorial Park Cemetery, Glendale. (Alan Arkin played him in the film And Starring Pancho Villa as Himself; year not confirmed.) The odd detail: a man who survived three armies' machine guns died by a medical error in a Los Angeles hospital — and had once run a fake medical office in Juárez to kidnap a prisoner.",
