      "summary": "Augusto César Sandino was the illegitimate son of a landowner, Gregorio Sandino, and an indigenous servant, Margarita Calderón. After shooting Dagoberto Rivas in 1921 he fled to Honduras, Guatemala and then Mexico, where he worked at an oil refinery near Tampico (Wikipedia says a Standard Oil refinery; I have not confirmed the company). In Mexico he took part in the Seventh-day Adventist church, spiritist circles and anti-imperialist groups, and became a member of the Magnetic-Spiritualist School of the Universal Commune (EMECU), founded in 1911 in Buenos Aires by the Spanish-born (Cintruenigo, Navarre) electrician Joaquín Trincado, a mixture of anarchism, Zoroastrianism, Kabbalah and Spiritism. He came home in 1926, in the middle of the Constitutionalist War. The odd detail: the future guerrilla leader learned his anti-imperialism in the oilfields of the enclave the setting makes American.",
