      "summary": "Born in Castellammare del Golfo in 1891, Magaddino became Buffalo's boss in 1922 and ran his bootlegging across the Niagara River behind a real funeral home. After repeal his family took in loan sharking, gambling and rackets across upstate New York, Pennsylvania, Ohio and Canada as far as Montreal. In 1936 a bomb meant for him killed his sister instead. Joseph Bonanno was his kinsman; later he attended the 1946 Havana conference and the 1957 Apalachin meeting. The odd detail: A Mafia boss who was, in daylight, an undertaker — the business with the best excuse for moving bodies.",
