      "summary": "On the night of 5–6 July 1922 the federal army attacked the tenants' union. Authorities recorded 4 dead and 22 wounded; the tenants said many more were killed, some buried inside the Cuartel Morelos (unverified — V_M09: efacico says the troops returned to the Cuartel Morelos and that bodies were buried at the Inalámbrica-station garrison (Parque Zaragoza)) and others thrown into the sea (efacico: at Playa Norte and Villa del Mar). In 1926 the union's new secretary-general Inés Terán published a manifesto claiming 150 dead. Proal was arrested [and \"83 union members\" — UNVERIFIED — V_M09; libcom says Marín was accused of homicide and sedition \"along with Proal and approximately ninety men and fifty women\"]; María Luisa Marín was charged with homicide and sedition (eleven months' incarceration, per libcom). The officer who ordered the repression, per efacico, was Col. Aarón López Manzano, after a clash at the Ferrer Guardia park in which two soldiers were mortally wounded; Gen. Guadalupe Sánchez's role in the attack is not confirmed (he was Veracruz's rebel commander in 1923). The odd detail: the official count was four; the union's was 150 — and the difference, they said, was in the barracks' ground and the harbour.",
