      "summary": "The anarchist leader (see the Baja entry) was arrested in Los Angeles in 1918 after an anti-war manifesto in Regeneración and sentenced under the Espionage Act of 1917 to twenty years for \"obstructing the war effort.\" He was 48, diabetic and going blind. He died in his cell on 21 November 1922. The cause is disputed: some say the guards murdered him; others medical neglect. U.S. authorities at first refused Mexico's request to send the body home; it was returned and interred in 1945 in the Rotunda of Illustrious Persons in Mexico City. The odd detail: he had warned in a letter that his pen, his \"only weapon,\" would become \"as useless as a broken sword\" — and the government that jailed him for it then refused to give the body back for three years.",
