      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "Outside Chicago, where the Municipal Court had replaced them, justices of the peace still sat — and signed permits to carry revolvers for \"self-protection\". After Frank Capone's death (1924) and a 1923 inquiry by the State's Attorney into where gangsters got revolver permits, the Survey records that permits held by the Capones had been signed by Justices George Miller and Emil Fisher of Cicero, and were revoked.",
