      "summary": "Bankrupt since 1917 (it sold its Chicago College of Medicine and Surgery to Loyola), the university lost its 1860 Old College Building to fire in 1923 and could not afford to clear the ruins. President Horace M. Evans, facing a $375,000 debt, tried the Rockefeller Foundation, rich donors and the Indiana legislature — and then almost sold the university to the Ku Klux Klan; the deal was stopped over \"legal technicalities\", a phrase the page suggests was used \"to save face for both organizations\". In July 1925 the Lutheran University Association (Missouri Synod) bought it. The odd detail: For a few months in 1923 the Klan came within a signature of owning a university an hour from Chicago.",
