      "summary": "Standard Oil built it \"for the city of Whiting\" in 1923 (architects Shattuck & Layer); the search-result summary puts the funding at $500,000, given jointly by the company and John D. Rockefeller and Rockefeller Jr., and the dedication on 12 November 1923 under Mayor Walter Schrage (confirmed on the Whiting-Robertsdale Historical Society page, https://www.wrhistoricalsociety.com/new-page-86, which also says the building was a memorial to First World War veterans, with an American Legion Post 80 placard at the dedication). The two-storey steel-frame building in rough red brick has an auditorium, meeting rooms, an indoor running track, gyms, lockers, a bowling alley and a swimming pool. It was the original home of the professional Whiting Ciesar All-Americans basketball team (Midwest Basketball Conference and the National Basketball League) before the team moved to Hammond. It also hosted the 1929 stockholders' meeting above. The odd detail: A company town built a gymnasium complex big enough to hold a Fortune 500 shareholders' meeting and a pro basketball team.",
