      "summary": "Rockford's early-1920s reputation for strict enforcement made it profitable: bootleggers from across the state came for the higher prices. The first gangland killing was Louis J. Milani, 8 October 1923, shot and dumped in a culvert near Montague Road (unsolved). Tom Perra vanished on 30 January 1928 after offering to inform, and was found shot near New Milford on 6 February. Antonio \"Tony\" Musso (Capone-connected, married into the Lombardo family) organised the bootlegging gangs c. 1927–28; Capone sent Nicolo Licata to help him. Joe Giovingo was killed on 14 August 1930 at Morgan and South Main by a shotgun from a big Dodge sedan — 17 wounds, killed within minutes; a funeral of over 1,500 with a 150-car procession. The folk story: Capone telephoned Joe's mother to apologise that the target had been Tony Abbott (Abbatini), a Capone associate hiding in Rockford who was in the car. Jack DeMarco came home from Leavenworth and was shot at his own welcome-home party on 20 January 1932 by three well-dressed men posing as police — never solved. Paul Giovingo was shot on 12 February 1933 on Winnebago Street: car forced to the kerb, ignition off, brake set, eight slugs in the left side, four to the head, after a warning letter; police met \"a wall of silence.\" By 1933 Musso held the town's liquor traffic. The odd detail: The Rockford gang's killers arrived dressed as police, and the murdered man's welcome-home party was under way in the next room.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High for dates and addresses (Haunted Rockford draws on the papers); Medium for the Capone-phone-call story (folk, one source). A fourth killing shown in one summary as 11 Feb 1933 is dated 12 Feb by the two page-reads; take 12 Feb.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — Musso is the man to whom Capone's Chicago Outfit (the Secret Service \"knew what Capone was\") subcontracts the northwest road. Four unsolved killings in a decade in a town of gospel Swedes: a GM's spine for a cult that pays the Outfit's bootleggers for silence about what is in a still-house in the culvert country.",
