      "summary": "The Jesuit college founded in 1886 as St. Ignatius College changed its name in May 1923 to \"Cleveland University\" and then, in September 1923, to John Carroll University after the first American Catholic archbishop. The same year it bought land in University Heights. Construction began in 1931; the buildings were not ready for classes until 1935. Its graduate school admitted women from 1934. The odd detail: For four months in 1923 the IHS seat was called \"Cleveland University\" — a name that vanished from every record.",
