      "summary": "Gary's mayor Roswell O. Johnson (first elected 1913, defeated 1917 by William Hodges, back in 1921) ran a system in which illegal saloon and gambling-hall keepers paid \"bonds\" to the city and the money went to political campaign accounts. A federal Prohibition prosecution (US Attorney Homer Elliott) reached the courtroom in March 1923, with armed guards in the courthouse and federal marshals bringing Gary witnesses to Indianapolis by train from Union Station. The star witness's story: Gaspare (Gaspari) Monti and his wife Mary ran the Black & Tan Saloon; a raid found dynamite and liquor in a tunnel between their house and the saloon; on 12 March 1923 Monti was shot dead by a sawed-off shotgun outside his home, days before he was due to testify against Mayor Johnson and City Judge William Dunn; his widow testified in his place. Sentences: Johnson, Judge Dunn and fifty-three other Lake County officials went to federal prison (a separate line of the same source says \"over six dozen\") (unverified — V_R37: the count is single-blog and self-contradicting; the Indiana Historical Bureau (https://blog.history.in.gov/the-case-of-agnes-szabo-bootlegger-entrepreneur-whistleblower/) confirms only \"over sixty officials were indicted,\" including Johnson and Judge Dunn); Johnson left Atlanta in November 1925. The odd detail: A tunnel between a house and a saloon holding dynamite, and a shotgun killing on the eve of testimony — in a city whose mayor was, on paper, the prosecution's defendant.",
      "evidence_status": "research lead",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: Medium (single blog; conviction counts vary within it). • Sentences: Johnson, Judge Dunn and fifty-three other Lake County officials went to federal prison (a separate line of the same source says \"over six dozen\") (unverified — V_R37: the count is single-blog and self-contradicting; the Indiana Historical Bureau (https://blog.history.in.gov/the-case-of-agnes-szabo-bootlegger-entrepreneur-whistleblower/) confirms only \"over sixty officials were indicted,\" including Johnson and Judge Dunn);",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — A tunnel between a house and a saloon on Adams Street — the setting's occult cell could run a whole cellar network under the \"Black & Tan\" rows south of Broadway, and the Gary rum case is the reason nobody looked.",
