      "summary": "The Valley Gang, an Irish street gang formed in the 1890s around Maxwell Street, became the Druggan-Lake beer organisation, owning several breweries by the early 1920s with partner Joseph Stenson. Sentenced to a year in 1924, Druggan and Lake bribed Sheriff Peter Hoffman and Warden Wesley Westbrook to let them come and go from Cook County Jail; after a Chicago American exposé Hoffman was fined $2,500 and jailed for a month, and Westbrook got four months. Wilson's Treasury unit convicted them of tax evasion in 1932, and the gang was absorbed into the Outfit by the end of Prohibition. Druggan retired rich — estates on Lake Zurich and in Florida, a racing stable — and died March 4, 1954. The odd detail: The sheriff went to jail for letting the prisoners out.",
