      "summary": "The daughter of Governor Joseph Fifer (elected 1889), Bohrer (born Bloomington 24 January 1877) was elected in 1924 as the first woman in the Illinois Senate and sat until 1932. She sponsored twenty child-welfare bills, half of which passed; a Dance Hall Bill limiting the halls' hours; the state-park system; \"Illinois\" as the state song; and a Midwife Bill that failed. She died 20 July 1960. The odd detail: The woman senator's signature law regulated the dance halls — the taxi-dance world of R16 was policed under a bill written by a governor's daughter from Bloomington.",
