      "summary": "Jim and Marian Jordan of Peoria (married 31 Aug 1918; met at church choir) came to Chicago radio in 1924 on WIBO's The Oh Henry! Twins, did farm-report comedy at WENR from 1927, and from April 1931 played Smackout on WMAQ — a fifteen-minute daily about a general store always \"smack out\" of everything; Marian voiced 69 characters. NBC took Smackout nationally 1933–35; Fibber McGee and Molly debuted on NBC from Chicago on 16 Apr 1935 at the urging of Henrietta Johnson Lewis, and S. C. Johnson's wax company took ownership of the names \"Fibber McGee\" and \"Molly\" as part of the deal. The show left for Hollywood in January 1939; the hall-closet gag dates only from 5 Mar 1940. The odd detail: the sponsor owned the characters' names — the Jordans could not be Fibber and Molly without Johnson's Wax.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — A company that owns a name. The Golden Circle's lawyers understand the trick; a name owned is a name that can be bound.",
