      "summary": "North Side boss Dean O'Banion ran the Schofield Flower Shop directly across from the cathedral and was shot there on Capone's orders in Nov 1924; the archdiocese refused his family a funeral Mass in the cathedral. On 11 Oct 1926 his successor Hymie (Earl) Weiss was cut down by two snipers outside the same shop; stray bullets struck the cathedral. Weiss received the last rites on the cathedral steps — and was also refused a cathedral funeral. The 1874–75 Keely Gothic building replaced its rectory with a six-storey block in 1929. Cardinals' red galeros hang from its ceiling, Mundelein's first among them. The odd detail: The cathedral itself was scarred by gangland bullets; a gangster was anointed on its steps and then refused its door.",
