      "summary": "The national WCTU had been run from Evanston since 1910; at its peak in 1927 it had more than 766,000 dues-paying members. Ella Boole led it from 1925 to 1933 and Ida B. Wise Smith from 1933 to 1944 — through the return of 3.2 beer on 7 April 1933 and full repeal on 5 December 1933 (R16). Membership fell to 372,355 by 1931 and 216,843 by 1941; the article notes only that membership declined once Prohibition was in force, and says little about how the Evanston headquarters met repeal. The odd detail: The largest women's organisation in the country lost half its members before repeal, not after — the victory emptied it.",
