      "summary": "D. C. Stephenson, Grand Dragon of the Indiana Klan and the most powerful man in the state (\"I am the law in Indiana\"), lured Madge Oberholtzer (28, manager of the state's Young People's Reading Circle) to his house on 15 Mar 1925 and, with bodyguards Earl Gentry and Earl Klinck, forced her onto his private compartment on the Chicago train, where he raped her and bit her repeatedly. They got off at Hammond and took rooms at the Indiana Hotel; she bought mercuric chloride tablets and swallowed three before vomiting. Driven home, she gave a dying declaration; she died 14 Apr 1925 of infection and kidney failure. Convicted of second-degree murder at Noblesville (unverified — V2_R06) on 14 Nov 1925; life. Denied parole in 1926, he handed his \"black boxes\" (unverified — V2_R06) of bribery records to the Indianapolis Times, destroying Governor Ed Jackson and collapsing the Indiana Klan from 250,000 to 4,000 by 1928. The odd detail: The bites. Her declaration described a man who \"chewed\" her (unverified — V2_R06); the period press did not need the word vampire to print it.",
