      "summary": "Touching down at 12:45 p.m. and dying at 4:30, the tornado ran 219 miles in 3 hours 45 minutes at an average 59 mph (73 through Murphysboro), over 1.5 miles wide in Hamilton County. 695 dead (12 Missouri, 588 Illinois, 95 Indiana), 2,027–2,756 injured, 15,000 homes gone, 57 schools damaged or destroyed — 33 children in the De Soto school alone; Murphysboro lost 234, West Frankfort 102 and its Caldwell mining village 43; Parrish was wiped out and never rebuilt; Griffin, Indiana, had not \"a single structure left untouched.\" It looked like \"amorphous rolling fog\" or \"boiling clouds,\" came after a day of only 69°F with snow flurries before, hid in rain and hail, and no photograph or film of it is known to exist. $16.55 million damage. The odd detail: the deadliest tornado in American history was never photographed and did not look like a tornado.",
