      "summary": "Machado ordered a model prison on the panopticon plan: five circular blocks of cells in tiers round a central watch-tower, built 1926–1931, for up to 5,000 prisoners. Its place in legend is later (Fidel and Raúl Castro were held there 1953–55, in the hospital wing), but it was the decade's showpiece of Machado's order, on the island where Americans had farmed grapefruit and waited for annexation. The odd detail: a prison designed so every prisoner is always possibly watched — Bentham's machine, built on Cuba's \"Treasure Island\".",
