      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "Folklore account: Two French officers in the 1740s or 1750s quarrelled over a woman; one killed the other, cut off the head, threw it into Lake Ontario and dropped the body down the well in the French Castle's first-floor room; the headless officer is said to walk under a full moon. The British filled the well in and covered it, fearing the French had poisoned it; caretakers reconstructed it in the 1920s.",
