      "summary": "The New York Central and the Pullman Company repainted seven Pullman cars in cardinal red and gold to carry the papal legate Cardinal Bonzano, Cardinal Hayes of New York, and seven visiting foreign cardinals and their entourages to the Congress. It left Grand Central at 10 a.m. on Wednesday 16 June 1926, made 8 stops so the faithful could greet the cardinals (unverified — V_R05), and reached Chicago in almost exactly 24 hours, where Mayor Dever, the City Council, Cardinal Mundelein and thousands met it. Afterwards the cars were repainted and put back into ordinary service — which is why few remember it. The odd detail: Seven cardinal-red Pullmans went back into ordinary service under plain paint — any sleeper on a 1930s New York Central run could be one of them.",
