      "summary": "The Jewish Charities withheld funds from the Orthodox Moses Montefiore Hebrew school to force it to accept the Charities' education-committee standards (chairman Dr. Alexander M. Dushkin), and pressed the Marks Nathan Jewish Orphan Home to accept $10,000 in county aid, which the home resisted. Rabbi Saul Silber (of Anshe Sholom; president of the Hebrew Theological College — R05) answered: \"Stopping the budget is an autocratic idea. It is neither Jewish nor American … Forcing starvation will not help us attain the goal.\" The Reform Rabbi Felix A. Levy backed the committee — if Dushkin approved, \"it must be all right.\" The fight fed accusations that the Reform-dominated Charities meant to suppress Orthodoxy in Chicago. The odd detail: An orphanage refusing $10,000 of county money rather than bend to its richer co-religionists.",
