      "summary": "The Ciudad Blanca (White City, also linked to a \"monkey god\") has been sought since the 16th century — Hernán Cortés's 1526 letter to the emperor mentions a Honduran region rumoured to exceed Mexico in riches. In 1927 the aviator Charles Lindbergh reportedly saw a \"white city\" while flying over eastern Honduras. In 1940 the American explorer Theodore Morde returned from La Mosquitia with thousands of artifacts and declared he had found the city, with a buried monkey-god statue; he never returned or gave the location, and Douglas Preston's 2017 The Lost City of the Monkey God concludes from Morde's own journals that he never found ruins and fabricated the story. In 2015 a scientific team (lidar) found ruins that might be the city — two sites, not one. The odd detail: the American explorer who returned with the artifacts and no location and whose own diary refuted him.",
