      "summary": "A civil war (the Constitutionalist War) began 2 May 1926; on 7 May 213 naval personnel landed at Bluefields, by 24 January 1927 there were 400 Marines and by March about 2,000 troops under Gen. Logan Feland. In May 1927 Henry Stimson brokered the Tipitapa agreement — disarmament of the Liberals (the \"Pact of Espino Negro,\" 4 May 1927) and a promise of supervised elections in 1928. Sandino and about 200 men refused to surrender. The National Guard (Guardia Nacional) was established in 1927, trained by Marines; the U.S. supervised the elections (4 Nov 1928: José María Moncada won; 6 Nov 1932: Juan Bautista Sacasa won). The odd detail: the Americans built the force that would, in seven years, kill Sandino.",
