      "summary": "Andrew Kehoe, a farmer and school-board treasurer angry at the school tax and beaten in the April 1926 election for township clerk, spent months wiring dynamite and pyrotol under the school floors. On the morning of 18 May 1927 he killed his wife Nellie, blew up his farm, and at 8:45 an alarm-clock timer fired the north wing, killing 36 children and two teachers. He then drove his truck, loaded with dynamite and scrap metal, to the school and detonated it, killing himself, the superintendent, two other adults and a child. Rescuers found about 500 lb of unexploded charges in the south wing. Thirty-eight children and six adults dead in all. A sign on his fence read \"CRIMINALS ARE MADE, NOT BORN.\" The odd detail: The alarm clock, the fence sign, and the 500 lb that failed to fire.",
