      "summary": "María Luisa Josefa of the Most Blessed Sacrament (\"Mother Luisita,\" 1866–1937), foundress of the Carmelite Sisters of the Sacred Heart in Mexico, left in disguise on 20 June 1927 with Sisters Teresa Navarro and Margarita María Hernández after public worship had been forbidden; they crossed at Nogales on 23 June, reciting a Te Deum, and were received by Bishop John J. Cantwell in Los Angeles on 24 June. They lodged in Long Beach with a Mrs. Nicolasa (as spelled on the site: \"Nicolastia\") Flores; more sisters followed. The exile house became the Carmelite Sisters of the Most Sacred Heart of Los Angeles, with a TB sanatorium (Santa Teresita, opened 2 August 1930). She returned to Mexico in May 1930 in poverty and died in Guadalajara on 11 February 1937, receiving Benediction moments before death. Declared Venerable. The odd detail: the nuns fled Mexico in lay clothes and sang the Te Deum at the border crossing.",
