      "summary": "The Favorite, a small excursion boat running from Lincoln Park to the Municipal Pier (Navy Pier), was caught by a sudden heavy squall and capsized half a mile off North Avenue on 28 July 1927. Seventy-five women and children and six men went into the water with her; rescuers got more than fifty out, but 27 died — 16 children, 10 women and one man. Johnny Weissmuller — the Olympic swimmer, then a Chicago lifeguard, later Tarzan — was one of the rescuers and is credited with pulling eleven people from the water (some accounts say with his brother Peter). The odd detail: A pleasure boat full of children capsizing in sight of the Gold Coast's windows on a summer afternoon, and a future movie Tarzan swimming out to it.",
