      "divergence": "BENDS — Coolidge is never president in the setting. In November 1927 the president is Charles Dawes (Wood died August 1927). So a Chicago banker signs Garvey's commutation and deportation. The Bureau case against Garvey (1919–23) ran in the years K. Edgar Hoover rose to Director (c. 1924). And if Jamaica is American by 1927, \"deportation\" is impossible — Garvey would be a colonial subject shipped home inside the same empire, or exiled elsewhere; if Jamaica is still British (proposal below), the record holds as written.",
