      "summary": "\"Anna Ecklund\" (pseudonym; real name Emma Schmidt), born in Milwaukee and raised around Marathon, Wisconsin, had been exorcised once before, on 18 June 1912. In 1928 the Bavarian-born Capuchin Fr. Theophilus Riesinger — formerly of St. Anthony's friary in Marathon, WI — exorcised her again at the Earling convent with the local pastor Fr. Joseph Steiger: she arrived 17 Aug; sessions ran 18–26 Aug, 13–20 Sept, and a last eight-day session 15–23 Dec 1928. Claimed phenomena: revulsion at holy objects, levitation, unknown languages, refusal of food. The demons were said to name themselves as Beelzebub, Judas Iscariot, her father Jacob and her aunt Mina. Theologian Carl Vogl published the account as Begone, Satan! (1935); Time ran it in 1936. The odd detail: The final session ended on 23 December 1928 — solstice week; the \"demons\" included her own dead father and aunt, who were blamed for cursing her.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
