      "summary": "The great Methodist church (congregation 1818; United Church of Canada from 1925) was largely destroyed by fire in 1928; only the tower, parts of the south façade and parts of the entrance porches survived. The congregation rebuilt on the old foundations to J. Gibb Morton's design with Massey family money and reopened in Dec 1929 with about 900 seats; Canada's largest pipe organ went in in 1930. The tower's carillon — 23 Gillett & Johnston bells installed 2 April 1922 — survived; they are inscribed \"May the spirit of the Lord reach the heart of every one where the sound of these bells is heard.\" The odd detail: The fire took the church and left the bell tower and its bells untouched.",
