      "summary": "John Griswold White (10 August 1845 – 26 August 1928), a Cleveland lawyer and CPL board president 1913–28, gave the library more than 60,000 books on Orientalia, folklore and related subjects and bequeathed a 12,000-volume chess and checkers collection, leaving the bulk of his estate to endow the John G. White Collection. He never married, died at Jackson, Wyoming, and is buried at Lake View. The odd detail: One of the great folklore libraries of the world sat in a Cleveland public building, open to anyone with a card — through the decade of the Torso murders.",
