      "divergence": "BENDS — Coolidge was never president in the setting. Leonard Wood died in 1927; Charles Dawes (a Chicago banker) was president 1927–29 and Hoover followed in 1929, so the 1928 Summer White House on the Brule would be Dawes's, and the man who endorsed Hoover on the school steps on 16 July would be a Chicagoan. Whether Dawes fished a northern trout stream is the owner's call; the infrastructure (depot, wires, an airport) and the Superior high school are exactly what a real summer presidency needed.",
