      "summary": "Illinois hanged its condemned until 1928; thereafter Cook County's death sentences were carried out in the county jail's electric chair — used 67 times between 1928 and the state's last electrocution (James Dukes, 24 August 1962 — the Wikipedia jail page misspells him \"Duke\"; see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_people_executed_in_the_United_States_in_1962). The new jail and Criminal Courts at 26th & Cal replaced the old Hubbard Street courthouse and jail in 1929. So in the 1930s a man condemned in Chicago was executed in the same complex where he was tried. The odd detail: trial, cell and death chair under one roof at 26th and California.",
