      "summary": "A 14-year-old Cristero flag-bearer, captured after giving his horse to his general, was handed to federal deputy Rafael Picazo and locked in the baptistry of his own parish church — which the soldiers had turned into a chicken coop, with fighting cocks tied at the main altar (he is said to have wrung their necks). Ordered to renounce his faith, he refused; the soldiers flayed the soles of his feet, made him walk on salt to the cemetery, and shot him there on 10 February 1928. Beatified 2005, canonized 16 October 2016. The odd detail: the fighting cocks at the altar — a church used as a cockpit.",
