      "divergence": "BENDS — and the setting has not said whether Baja California is ceded. Baja is not on the ceded list, but ALTERNATE_HISTORY §7.4 puts Mexicali's Colorado-delta cotton among the northern prizes. If Baja stays Mexican (recommended), the resort holds: it is the point of the border — American vice beyond American law, run by a Sonoran governor (Rodríguez was born in Guaymas, ceded Sonora). If Baja is ceded, Tijuana is American soil and a casino there is illegal, so Agua Caliente would need to be a licensed concession. Prohibition itself holds (repeal Dec 1933, domestic calendar), so the 1928–33 vice economy is intact either way.",
