      "summary": "The Medinah Athletic Club placed a copper box of organizational records in its cornerstone on 5 November 1928. A contemporary Tribune report lists membership records, officers’ pictures, coins and a consistory Bible among the contents. The club opened in 1929 with lavish historically themed interiors and a celebrated fourteenth-floor pool. A later Tribune architectural account describes athletic facilities, smoking lounges and restrictions that routed women separately to the ballroom. Bankruptcy followed in 1934. This combines a tangible time capsule with patronage, exclusion, extraordinary engineering and the abrupt financial reversal of a prestigious institution.",
