      "summary": "The year's sequence, from Wikipedia's page on the Temple: on 15 March 1929 Claude Green-Bey, the temple's business manager, who had split off after a funds dispute and declared himself Grand Sheik, was stabbed to death at Unity Hall on Indiana Avenue. Noble Drew Ali died at home on 20 July 1929, aged 43; the death certificate says \"tuberculosis broncho-pneumonia,\" and followers speculated otherwise. On 25 September 1929 Chicago police, investigating the reported kidnapping of Charles Kirkman Bey by Ira Johnson, were met by gunfire from Johnson's house. The fight spilled into the neighbourhood: a policeman and a member were killed and a second policeman died later of his wounds. Police took 60 people into custody (R05 records the Tribune headline \"Seize 60 After So. Side Cult Tragedy\") and a reported 1,000 officers patrolled the South Side that night. Three men then claimed the succession: Edward Mealy El (named by Drew Ali), John Givens El (who claimed to be Drew Ali reincarnated) and Charles Kirkman Bey (named Grand Advisor by the governors). The odd detail: A founder dies, and within ten weeks a \"kidnapping\" turns into a firefight in which two policemen die — and one claimant says the founder has been reborn in him.",
