      "summary": "President Herbert Hoover set up the National Commission on Law Observance and Enforcement on 20 May 1929; its 14-volume report came out in 1931 (final report 7 Jan 1931). The volume Lawlessness in Law Enforcement found \"the inflicting of pain, physical or mental, to extract confessions or statements ... is widespread throughout the country\"; the police volume (August Vollmer its principal author) condemned the police's \"general failure ... to detect and arrest criminals guilty of the many murders, spectacular bank, payroll and other holdups\". The odd detail: a federal commission put in print, in 1931, that American police routinely tortured suspects — and nothing changed in the station houses.",
