      "synopsis": "The American anthropologist Elsie Clews Parsons (1875–1941) spent three field seasons in Mitla and published Mitla, Town of the Souls with the University of Chicago Press in 1936. She records that the old Zapotec name Lyobaa means \"Place of Tombs\", and that \"the souls, las ánimas, of all Zapotecan people, from valley and mountain come to Mitla\"; that \"witches and spirits as well as robbers are abroad at night\";…",
