      "summary": "Robert S. Abbott's Defender (founded 1905), carried south by Pullman porters against southern law, had been the Great Migration's recruiting sheet; in 1928 it refused for the first time to endorse the Republican presidential candidate. In 1929 Abbott and editor Lucius Harper created the Bud Billiken Club on the \"Junior Defender\" page and the same year the Bud Billiken Parade and Picnic, still held on the South Side every August. At its peak each copy was read by four or five people. Abbott's nephew John H. Sengstacke took over in 1940. The odd detail: a newspaper distributed by railway porters, illegal to sell in parts of the South, with a children's parade as its public face.",
