      "summary": "Mella, the student leader who founded the University Students' Federation (FEU, 1922) and the first Cuban Communist Party (1925), was expelled from the University of Havana in 1925, went on a hunger strike, and fled Machado in early 1926. On 10 January 1929 he was shot at point-blank range while walking home with the photographer Tina Modotti. Suspects ever since: Machado's agents, Comintern operatives, or the Italian communist gunman Vittorio Vidali; historians have no consensus. His ashes came home in 1933; troops broke up the reburial and about six people were shot. The odd detail: a murder with three candidate killers and one eyewitness — a photographer, who was arrested and put on trial in the press herself.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High.",
