      "confidence": "High on the outline (a single local-history article; figures as given).",
      "confidence_level": "High",
      "unverified": [],
      "divergence": "BENDS — Teapot Dome was Harding's Interior Secretary's scandal (1922–23); with Harding never president the Fall bribe can't exist as such (Wood is president 1921–27). Continental Trading and Stewart's obstruction can hold, but the Continental profits were paid out in Liberty Bonds, a First World War instrument, so the payoff cannot hold as written in a timeline with no U.S. war loans; and Teapot Dome must be replaced by a setting equivalent; the Rockefeller/Standard Oil corporate fight holds.",
