      "summary": "In the early hours of May 8, 1929 the bodies of John Scalise, Albert Anselmi and Joseph \"Hop Toad\" Giunta were found near Hammond. All three had been savagely beaten and shot; one wound had torn off Scalise's left little finger, and the coroner said he had never seen such disfigured bodies. The North Side gang was suspected at first but cleared within days. Years later the \"more popular story\" emerged: Capone invited them to a banquet and beat them with a baseball bat before gunmen finished them. The odd detail: The baseball-bat banquet — the scene every film uses — is a later story; the record has only the bodies and the coroner's horror.",
