      "summary": "Organised by Meyer Lansky — on his honeymoon — with Johnny Torrio, Lucky Luciano and Frank Costello, and hosted by Atlantic City boss Enoch \"Nucky\" Johnson, the conference brought bosses together to discuss bootleg competition in New York and Chicago, plans for repeal, a shift into bookmaking, racing and casinos, and a national structure. Chicago sent Al Capone, Frank Nitti, Jake Guzik, Frank Rio and Frank McErlane. Afterwards Capone and Rio went to Philadelphia, where \"two friendly police officers\" arrested them for carrying guns (May 16, 1929) — the year in Eastern State followed. The odd detail: The first American mob summit was held because the Breakers hotel wouldn't take them — and it ended with Capone arranging his own arrest.",
