      "summary": "A storm that crawled over Nassau and Andros at 2–3 mph and held hurricane force there for about 48 hours (25–26 September 1929), with gusts of 164 mph at Nassau and a surge of 12+ feet reaching 20 miles inland on Andros. It destroyed 73% of Nassau's homes and businesses, left 5,000+ homeless, killed 142 in the Bahamas (35 on the schooner Pretoria off Fresh Creek) and 13 in the US; it wrecked about 70% of the sponging fleet and nearly all the sponge warehouses. A fungus later killed ~99% of the sponges and ended the colony's staple trade. The tanker Potomac logged 924 mb; the storm spawned some of the first verified hurricane tornadoes in Florida. The odd detail: the storm ran south-west, the wrong way, and sat on the colony for two days — the kind of storm people say was sent.",
