      "summary": "The first sitting British Prime Minister to visit the United States landed in New York on 4 October 1929 (ticker-tape parade the same day), went by train to Washington for a 20-minute first meeting with Hoover, retreated with him to Rapidan Camp on 5 October for naval-disarmament talks, and on 7 October addressed the Senate for 20 minutes on peace and disarmament. He crossed into Canada at Niagara Falls on 15 October, reached Toronto, met Mackenzie King in Ottawa on 17 October and sailed from Quebec on 25 October — the day after Black Thursday. Chicago was not on the route. The odd detail: The one week a British Prime Minister spent in North America straddled the Crash, and he left the continent from Quebec the day after the market broke.",
