      "summary": "Eight days before the Crash, Ford staged the fiftieth anniversary of Edison's electric lamp in the Menlo Park laboratory he had moved from New Jersey — library, machine shop and seven railway cars of New Jersey soil. President Herbert Hoover and Lou Henry Hoover, Marie Curie, George Eastman, Andrew Mellon, John D. Rockefeller Jr., Will Rogers and Orville Wright attended; Einstein spoke by radio. Edison re-enacted the moment by connecting two wires, broadcast over about 140 stations, while Americans were urged to switch their lights off and back on together. Edison, overcome, said the lab was cleaner than the original. On 16 April 1938 Ford added the Wright brothers' home and bicycle shop to the village, with Orville Wright present. The odd detail: Seven freight cars of New Jersey dirt, so the laboratory would stand on its own ground.",
