      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the figures and institutions; the mosque's exact address and founding minister UNVERIFIED. • The Nation of Islam's Muhammad Mosque Number Three opened on McKinley Boulevard in 1935 — Milwaukee's temple was the third in the movement, after Detroit and Chicago. (unverified — V_R27)",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — A community small enough that everyone knows who is new — and a Mosque No. 3 whose founder, in the archive's C08/C09 thread, vanished in 1934. The Milwaukee temple is where the Chicago question (\"where did Fard go?\") is asked in a city with no Black policemen to ask it.",
