      "summary": "Cuba's first shopping arcade, built on part of the old city wall's moat and foundations, planned by Don Julián de Zulueta (1873 origins), designed by Pedro Tomé y Veracruisse (construction began 1890), finished by Andrés Gómez Mena, with four floors added 1916–18 — eight elevators, an X-shaped plan of interior passages, 560 offices (law firms, consular and diplomatic agencies), the Pitman commercial academies, and the Ibero-American Institution of Culture chaired by Fernando Ortiz. About 25,000 people passed through daily. It housed two short-lived theatres (the Politeama Grande and Pequeño). The odd detail: Andrés Gómez Mena was shot dead in Havana on 11 January 1917 by a Catalan watchmaker, Fernando Reugart, who \"argued that Gómez Mena had disrespected his wife\" — one month before the Marines landed. The arcade's four diagonal streets \"form an X.\"",
