      "summary": "Havana's city of the dead: the Necrópolis de Cristóbal Colón, founded 1876 (first stone 30 October 1871; burials from 1868) to replace the Espada Cemetery, designed by the Galician Calixto de Loira (its first resident, who died before it was finished). About 50 hectares (620 by 800 m), 500+ major mausolea, a Greek-cross plan with an octagonal Central Chapel modelled on the Florence Duomo; the entrance arch's group (Wikipedia: Faith, Hope and Charity by José Vilalta Saavedra; the 1922 guide says a Crucifixion panel by Saavedra topped by Columbus \"bringing the light of religion to the New World\"). Plots were assigned by class — areas for priests, soldiers, brotherhoods, the wealthy, the poor, infants, epidemic victims, \"pagans and the condemned.\" The Firemen's Monument (Agustín Querol; for the 28 firemen killed in the fire of 17 May 1890) \"cost $79,000\" (1941 guide). The Capilla del Amor — built by Juan Pedro Baró for his wife Catalina Lasa (the 1941 guide: \"one bereaved Cuban spent $150,000 on a mausoleum of Lalique crystal … to house the remains of his wife\"). The Students' Monument for the 1871 eight; the Tomb of Calixto García; a plot for the Maine's dead in 1898 (disinterred December 1899 for Arlington); baseball monuments (1942, 1951). An open-air flower market ran along 12th Street and 23rd (1941). The cemetery's extension was completed 1934. The odd detail: Wikipedia says remains are exhumed \"after three years … boxed and placed in a storage building.\" The 1941 guide flatly says the opposite: \"Don't believe the old wives' tale that when poor people can't afford to pay rent on graves, the bones are dug up. It isn't so.\" (The Espada system in the 1922 guide did rent niches and empty them into a bone-pit.) Havana's dead were a matter of rumour, and the sources disagree with each other.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High for the founding, design and figures; the exhumation rule is contested (as above). Catalina Lasa's death year and the tomb's date: UNVERIFIED here.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — Three layers: the officials' story (you can't dig them up), the poor's story (they do), and the fact — a storage building that nobody has ever counted. See M03: The Colón Cemetery; La Milagrosa; the ABC tunnel.",
