      "summary": "Trotsky arrived in Mexico in January 1937 and lived at the Casa Azul from January 1937 to April 1939, then at the Viena Street house from April 1939 to August 1940. After the 24 May 1940 attack — led, per the page, by Siqueiros and NKVD agent Iosif Grigulevich, men disguised as police machine-gunning the courtyard, Trotsky's grandson wounded in the foot, his young assistant/bodyguard Robert Sheldon Harte abducted and later murdered — high walls with watchtowers were built. The garden held rare cacti he collected, and rabbits and chickens. 20 August 1940: Ramón Mercader (\"Jacson Mornard\", Canadian passport) struck him with an alpine axe; he died 21 August. His ashes lie in a stele by Juan O'Gorman in the garden. The odd detail: The garden rabbits and chickens — a revolutionary who fed poultry in a walled compound with watchtowers.",
