      "summary": "Born April 28, 1906 on the Near West Side to Sicilian parents, Accardo left school at 14, joined Claude Maddox's and Tony Capezio's Circus Café Gang and was recruited by Jack McGurn. His nickname \"Joe Batters\" is credited to killing three traitors with a baseball bat (the article presents it as fact; compare the Scalise-Anselmi \"banquet\" story, which is legend). He later boasted on federal wiretaps of taking part in the St. Valentine's Day Massacre, which most experts doubt. Under Nitti he made money, got his own crew and became head of enforcement; in 1943 Ricca made him underboss, beginning a partnership of almost 30 years. The odd detail: The Outfit's longest-serving boss is remembered by a nickname from a baseball bat — and bragged into a government microphone about a massacre he probably missed.",
