      "summary": "Guy Warren Ballard (b. Newton, Kansas 28 July 1878), a mining promoter who had married Edna Anne Wheeler in Chicago in 1916, claimed that while hiking Mount Shasta in 1930 the Count of Saint Germain appeared, offered him a special drink, and began training him as a \"Messenger.\" Writing as \"Godfré Ray King\" he published Unveiled Mysteries (1934) and The Magic Presence; the movement grew fast through Chicago lectures, with members chanting \"decrees\" to the Ascended Masters. By 1938 the Ballards claimed about a million followers. Guy died 29 Dec 1939 at 61; the faithful said he had \"ascended\" and venerate him as Ascended Master Godfre. The odd detail: The founder of a movement promising physical ascension died a very physical death one week after the 1939 solstice — and his followers simply announced the ascension.",
