      "synopsis": "On December 30, 1903, fire during a matinee of Mr. Blue Beard killed 602 people, the worst theatre fire in U.S. history; many died in the icy alley behind, falling or jumping from fire escapes. The theatre reopened as Hyde & Behman's Music Hall (1904), became the Colonial, was demolished in 1925, and the Oriental Theatre rose on the site in 1926 — so in the 1930s a brand-new movie palace stood on the death site,…",
