      "summary": "The county poorhouse: opened about 1910 on 153 acres, with the remaining residents of Dunning moved here by July 1, 1911. Called variously the Cook County Poor Farm, Almshouse, Poorhouse — and the Oak Forest Tuberculosis Hospital. In the Depression it is the end of the road for the old, the sick and the penniless of Cook County. It was never annexed to any town — an island of county land. The odd detail: The poorhouse had its own burial ground for residents nobody claimed (UNVERIFIED from the page read — see Leads).",
