      "summary": "Opened March 28, 1929: the largest indoor arena in the world, 26,000 seats, with the world's largest theatre organ — a 3,663-pipe Barton, six keyboards, 800-plus stops. Its builder, boxing promoter Paddy Harmon, sank his whole fortune into it and died in a car crash within a year, leaving his widow the shares and $2.50. In 1932 both national conventions met here; FDR won the Democratic nomination here (and again in 1940 and 1944). Also 1932's first indoor NFL playoff game. The odd detail: The organ was so loud it gave the building its nickname.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
