      "summary": "Recruits were brought into a dark room among robed figures and made to kneel at gunpoint (a 1936 account: the sponsor \"held a loaded pistol to the supplicant's heart\") while swearing an oath that began: \"In the name of God and the Devil, one to reward and the other to punish… I pledge and consecrate my heart, my brain, my body, and my limbs…\". It bound them to the \"extermination\" of \"the Anarchist, Communist, the Roman Hierarchy,\" to obey superiors absolutely, and to accept torture rather than betray the order. Each initiate was given a bullet — the reminder of what awaited a traitor. Members wore black silk robes, pirate-style hats and a skull-and-crossbones insignia. The odd detail: the oath invokes God and the Devil by name — the Legion literally swears on the Devil as its enforcer.",
