      "summary": "The radio Annie began on WGN in 1930 and went to NBC Blue on 6 Apr 1931 (running to 26 Apr 1942); Ovaltine sponsored it 1930–40 and gave nearly seven minutes of each fifteen to the product. It invented radio premiums: the Radio Orphan Annie Secret Society, the shake-up mug, and from 1935 the annual decoder pins and badges redeemed with Ovaltine proofs of purchase. The decoded messages, against legend, were previews of coming episodes rather than commercials — the \"drink your Ovaltine\" joke is Jean Shepherd's (later A Christmas Story). Shirley Bell (Cole) was Annie; Stanley Andrews was Daddy Warbucks. The odd detail: hundreds of thousands of Chicago-region children owned a working cipher badge and used it every night.",
