      "divergence": "BENDS — the visit's whole frame is Soviet: in 1927 he had been jailed in Leningrad, \"accused of counter-revolutionary activities, and sentenced to death,\" then exiled and released to Riga under Western pressure (Hoover had lobbied for him). The setting has no Soviet Union. The tour and the Hoover meeting can stand (Hoover is president 1929–33 in the setting too), but who persecuted him in a defeated, reparations-paying Russia is the owner's call. His 1940 rescue from Warsaw also falls away with Nazi Germany.",
