      "summary": "The John G. Shedd Aquarium opened to large crowds on 30 May 1930, although its benefactor had died in 1926 before construction began. Shedd’s institutional history traces the project from his initial donation and the aquarium society through groundbreaking in November 1927 and the 1930 opening. The result was a substantial new educational institution created through wealthy patronage during a rapidly worsening economy. Its original marble building is the period anchor. Later additions materially changed its scale and layout, so a modern exterior photograph should be annotated before it becomes a source for a 1930s game location.",
