      "summary": "George Stathakis, a Greek immigrant cook in Buffalo, went over the Falls in a barrel on 4 July 1930 with an air supply of up to eight hours. The barrel was trapped behind the curtain of water for 18 hours; he suffocated. (Two years earlier, on 4 July 1928, Jean Lussier survived the drop inside a large rubber ball with a spring-steel frame; in 1920 the Englishman Charles Stephens died when his barrel's ballast tore through the bottom, leaving only his right arm in the harness.) The odd detail: He took his pet turtle, said to be about 150 years old. The turtle survived.",
