      "summary": "Jack Zuta — the North Side gang's accountant and political fixer, once a Madison Street brothel operator — was arrested and released after the Lingle murder, which he and Bugs Moran were alleged to have ordered after Lingle demanded a cut of their gambling. He fled to the Wisconsin lakes and lived as \"J. H. Goodman\". On August 1, 1930 he was shot to death in a Delafield roadhouse, most likely by the Capone organisation in revenge for Lingle. Zuta kept meticulous records; the papers later found in his safe-deposit boxes exposed kickbacks to officials and police raids on breweries. The odd detail: The gang's bookkeeper died, and his safe-deposit boxes kept talking after him.",
