      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the pamphlets, dates and the WPA project; sightings are period press as reported (one is a 2010s article citing the State Journal); the Geneva Lake 1902 item comes from a search-result summary. • and on Geneva Lake the Janesville Gazette of 29 September 1902 reported a snake-like creature 65 feet long and 8–10 inches thick. (unverified — V_R42)",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — An archive of local ghosts assembled by a museum man and a federal typist in 1936: the \"cases\" already exist as file cards. An investigator uses Brown's Ghost Tales as a gazetteer — and finds the first card that Brown did not print.",
