      "summary": "On 6 March 1931, before the 7 a.m. Mass, a dynamite bomb exploded in Xalapa Cathedral. The attack was never cleared up. Anticlerical circles said the Church had set it off itself; Catholics blamed the state's anticlerical faction; it fell in the year of Governor Adalberto Tejeda's law cutting the number of priests and of the 25 July shooting in the Veracruz port cathedral (M01). The source is a 2025 local-history piece citing a 2014 memoir by Rubén Pabello Rojas. The odd detail: the account calls it \"Monday 6 March 1931\"; 6 March 1931 was a Friday — a small error in the source, worth noting before anyone quotes the day.",
