      "summary": "Notre Dame's football coach, Norwegian-born and raised in Chicago, a convert from Lutheranism to Catholicism (20 November 1925), was flying to Los Angeles to work on the film The Spirit of Notre Dame when the TWA Fokker F-10 broke up in flight — its plywood wing, bonded with water-based glue, failed in rain. Eight died. President Hoover called it \"a national loss\"; over 100,000 lined the funeral route and the funeral was broadcast live nationwide and abroad. Studebaker sold a \"Rockne\" car 1931–33. The odd detail: The plane came apart because its glue dissolved in the rain.",
