      "summary": "Gary police called in \"Captain Thomas J. Callaghan of the United States secret service\" over what they took to be a \"mammoth counterfeiting scheme.\" A raid on \"Daum's room at the Washington hotel\" found \"masks, a pistol, blackface and fake stock certificates.\" Three men (Daum, Clayton and Martin) were held, and the scheme was said to include a plan to kidnap an unnamed person. Callaghan's ruling was that they could not be prosecuted for \"thinking\" about counterfeiting, since they had not acted on it. The odd detail: masks, a pistol and blackface in a hotel room: a disguise kit for a crime that never happened, and a Secret Service captain who declined to charge a thought.",
