      "summary": "Neighbors and Unemployed Council activists resisted the eviction of 72-year-old Diana Gross by putting her furniture back inside. Police confrontation followed and Black protesters were killed. Communist organizer Bill Gebert's contemporary account names Abe Gray, John O'Neil and Thomas Page and gives the address as 5016 South Dearborn. Later scholarship describes a wider aftermath of demonstrations centered on Washington Park. The incident joins housing insecurity, racial inequality, political organizing and sharply opposed newspaper narratives in one neighborhood-scale event.",
