      "summary": "The Belize hurricane of 10 September 1931 (about 2,500 dead per the Jesuit page; a search summary says roughly 70 percent of Belize City destroyed) demolished the twin pyramidal steeples of Holy Redeemer Cathedral — shorter replacements were blown away in later storms. At St. John's College, on the day of the St. George's Caye holiday, 33 died: 11 Jesuits, 18 students and 4 servants; \"not a stick left standing.\" The Jesuits: priests Francis Kemphues, Charles Palacio, Bernard New, Leo Rooney, John Tracy, William Ferris; scholastics Richard Koch, Alfred Baumeister, Deodato Burn, Richard Smith; brother John Rodgers. Father Kemphues absolved the dying despite a broken leg and a fractured skull. The odd detail: the school had moved to swampland in 1916; the hurricane came on a holiday.",
