      "summary": "The Purple Gang — Jewish bootleggers and hijackers led by Abe, Joe, Raymond and Izzy Bernstein — ran Canadian whisky across the river with \"the Little Jewish Navy\" and for years supplied Capone's Chicago. On 16 September 1931 three rival gangsters, Herman \"Hymie\" Paul, Isadore \"Joe\" Sutker and Joseph Lebowitz, were lured to a Collingwood apartment for a \"peace conference\" and shot dead. Raymond Bernstein, Irving Milberg and Harry Keywell were convicted of first-degree murder, and the convictions broke the gang; by 1932 it was finished as a power. (The 1927 \"Cleaners and Dyers War\" extortion case against nine Purples ended in acquittals.) The odd detail: On 13 February 1929 Abe Bernstein allegedly tipped Bugs Moran about a booze shipment — the bait that drew Moran's men to the garage on Clark Street the next morning.",
