      "collection": "Mexico & Caribbean",
      "synopsis": "Gaspar Yanga, an African (traditionally a Central African prince) who fled slavery around 1570, led a maroon settlement in the mountains near Córdoba; in 1609 it fought off a Spanish expedition, and by negotiation (c. 1618) his people won freedom and self-rule — San Lorenzo de los Negros, called the first free Black town in the Americas. In 1932 the municipality was renamed Yanga in his honour.",
