      "summary": "William Lyon Mackenzie King (Prime Minister 1921-30 and from October 1935; Leader of the Opposition in 1930-35, when the séances began in 1932), \"kept secret his beliefs in spiritualism and the use of mediums to stay in contact with departed associates, particularly with his mother,\" and this, Wikipedia says, distorted his understanding of Hitler. He first met Etta Wriedt, a \"direct-voice\" medium from Detroit, in 1932, through Mrs. Fulford, a senator's widow, at her Brockville home (first name (unverified — V_R40)); she held over 60 séances (unverified — V_R40: the pages read say 'several' at Brockville in February 1932 and 'dozens' of séances overall; none gives a Wriedt count) for him at Detroit, Laurier House, Kingsmere and Brockville, and at the first he was convinced he felt the presence of his parents, siblings, grandfather, Sir Wilfrid Laurier and his friend Bert Harper. Wriedt (born in Oswego, N.Y.; 1862–1942 in Wikipedia, 1859 in others) used a trumpet in darkened rooms and a spirit guide \"John Sharp,\" visited England five times (sitting with W. T. Stead and Vice-Admiral Usborne Moore), and was exposed by the Norwegian physicist Kristian Birkeland, who traced the noises to potassium and water and to lycopodium powder; Joseph McCabe reported a hidden telescopic aluminium tube. W. B. Yeats attended, doubted and was dropped. The odd detail: Mackenzie King (Leader of the Opposition to October 1935, then Prime Minister) travelled to Detroit through the 1930s for séances with a medium who had already been exposed in print — the Umbra circle of a head of government who believes.",
