      "summary": "Edith Rockefeller McCormick spent her final illness in the Drake after leaving her Lake Shore Drive mansion. TIME’s contemporary account describes visits by her former husband and children after family estrangement, and the presence of her companion Edwin Krenn. It is useful evidence for the hotel as a place of long-term elite residence, illness and private family negotiation rather than only public parties. Her story also intersects with opera patronage, real-estate reversals and collecting. The source’s sensational language should be treated as 1932 journalism, not adopted as a neutral description of her character.",
