      "summary": "Governor Victórico R. Grajales (Dec 1932 – 1936) ran an \"antialcohol and religious de-fanaticisation\" campaign through the state's Department of Social Action; one summary says he closed all the churches in Chiapas and forced the priests underground before the federal school reform of 1934. A study of the Zoque region reports that in Ocozocoautla, in November 1934, the municipal authorities closed the parish church and several hermitages, burned the religious images and ransacked the temple on the pretext of making it a school; images were also destroyed at Chiapilla, Jiquipilas, Tapilula and Copainalá. In Tapachula the church of San Agustín had been seized by the schismatic ICAM in 1926, and the federal government closed it in June 1932; petitions from several groups to convert it into a school were denied. By 1934, the only priest authorised to work in Chiapas was José Ramírez of the ICAM, at Ixtapa. The odd detail: the only licensed priest in a whole state was a schismatic one.",
