      "summary": "A magnitude-6.7 earthquake hit Santiago at about 1:15 a.m. on 3 February 1932 (one local page gives 1:12; the Spanish Wikipedia summary gives a 5 p.m. tremor — the sources conflict). The Cathedral's towers cracked and were thought likely to need demolition; the cathedral clock stopped at 1:14; the angel statue was damaged (local sources); the churches of Dolores and San Francisco were also badly damaged. About 80 percent of the city's buildings were affected; deaths are given as 8–14 (sources differ), injured about 300 (both Wikipedias; the local page says about 200; one source: nearly 2,000). The jail's prisoners were moved to the barracks. A local account says that on 10, 17 and 24 January Fathers Callejas and Cresencio Pajares told congregations of an approaching \"test.\" The odd detail: the priests' sermons before the quake — a period anecdote (not a verified prophecy) — and the stopped clock.",
