      "summary": "While Rivera painted at the DIA, Frida Kahlo, about three and a half months pregnant, began bleeding heavily on the night of 4 July 1932 and lost the child at Henry Ford Hospital. She painted Henry Ford Hospital (1932, oil on metal, 12 × 15 in.) — herself naked and weeping on a floating hospital bed, tied by red threads to six objects: the male foetus, a snail, a piece of medical machinery, a purple orchid Rivera had given her, a pelvis and an anatomical model — with the Detroit skyline and the River Rouge plant on the horizon. Obstetricians have called her anatomy \"strikingly accurate\". The odd detail: Ford's factory on the horizon of a painting of a miscarriage, in a hospital that bears Ford's name.",
