      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High (detailed Wikipedia page drawn from the Detroit Free Press coverage). R05 covers the movement; this is the killing only. • Fard's Allah Temple of Islam), led his boarder (unverified — V2_R06) James J. • It was predestined 1,500 years ago that at that hour I must make a human sacrifice.\" He said it was the first of twelve (unverified — V_R06), and had named a welfare worker who cut him from relief, and two judges, as future offerings. • The count — \"the ninth hour of the twentieth day,\" \"the first of twelve\" (unverified — V_R06) — and the underlined magazine story left open on the altar like a citation. • What the papers said: \"voodoo.\" What the folklore says: a \"king.\" What was really there: a schedule of twelve (unverified — V_R06).",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — A real Depression-era sacrifice with a calendar, an altar and a text — the owner's \"cult versus population\" in one Dubois Street house. What the papers said: \"voodoo.\" What the folklore says: a \"king.\" What was really there: a schedule of twelve (unverified — V_R06).",
