      "summary": "Italy was the most eager official foreign participant. Its pavilion was built in the plan of a giant aeroplane to commemorate Balbo's flight, with a façade of bundled fasces. Inside: 450 exhibits on engineering, physics, medicine, geography, astronomy, agriculture, shipping and aviation \"from the times of the Caesars to the present day,\" including the draining of the Pontine/Ostian marshes; Italy also had space in the Hall of Science, the Adler Planetarium and the Museum of Science and Industry. After the fair Italy \"generously donated the entire display to the Rosenwald Museum\" (MSI). Per Herman (2020), Italian-Americans at the fair \"were held in check by the close oversight of Fascist Italy's representatives.\" The odd detail: The one foreign government building with a party symbol on its face — and the fair and the State Department raised no objection.",
