      "summary": "Jerry Siegel (born Cleveland 17 October 1914, son of Lithuanian-Jewish immigrants) moved to Glenville in 1928, published \"the first sci-fi fanzine,\" Cosmic Stories, in 1929, and met the artist Joe Shuster at Glenville High (both graduated June 1934). On 2 June 1932 his father, Michael Siegel, a clothing-store owner, \"was punched hard in the chest by a shoplifter and suffered a fatal heart attack.\" In a self-published fanzine Jerry printed \"The Reign of the Superman,\" in which the Superman is a vagrant named Bill Dunn given psychic powers — a villain. The hero version followed; in March 1938 the boys sold Superman to Detective Comics for $130. The odd detail: The first \"Superman\" in Cleveland was a bread-line tramp turned into a telepathic tyrant by an experiment — written the year the writer's father died after a robbery.",
