      "summary": "Dawson, a Republican state central committeeman from 1930, was 2nd Ward alderman from 1933 to 1939. In 1938 he ran for Congress as a Republican against Mitchell and lost, 26,396 (46.63%) to 30,207; leaving the Council in 1939 he became a Democratic committeeman, and after 1952 the leader of the Black \"sub-machine\" inside the Cook County Democratic Organization, which for decades delivered the South Side wards — and, by long repute, protected the policy wheels (not stated in the source read). He died of pneumonia in Chicago on 9 November 1970. Wikipedia gives him service as a first lieutenant in the 366th Infantry, 1917–19. The odd detail: The man who would run Black Chicago's Democratic machine for thirty years spent the whole 1930s as a Republican and only crossed over when the votes did.",
