      "summary": "The Abendpost covered the Friends of the New Germany's Chicago district meetings (Aug and Oct 1934, \"large crowds\"; a tenth-anniversary district convention), a \"Deutsch Voelkischer Evening at Lake Shore Athletic Club\" (June 1935) and a Saar demonstration (Dec 1934). On 10 Dec 1936 WPA interviewer Dr. Harvey Wish recorded Dr. Hugo Ferdinand Simon, former German Consul General, at 443 Barry Ave.: he described \"the rapid conversion recently of many Chicago Germans to supporters of the Hitler Government,\" called \"the Jewish question\" a purely German matter, and said German Chicago still kept few ties even to Milwaukee. Secondary sources (not opened this session) report a Bund meeting of ~1,000 at the Germania Club in Feb 1938, a counter-protest of 3,000+ at Lincoln Turner Hall in Oct 1938 against a Bund Sudetenland rally, and a Bund picnic of 4,000–8,000 in present-day Merrimac Park on 18 June 1939 (unverified — V_R15). The odd detail: the WPA interviewer's own aside, typed into the record: the effect of the new orientation \"remains to be seen, and very shortly.\"",
