      "summary": "Insull's Chicago Civic Opera folded in 1932 (see R08). The Chicago Grand Opera Company took the house for 1933–35 and went bankrupt; the Chicago City Opera Company was \"organized from the remaining assets\" and gave four seasons, 1935 to 1939, \"before it too succumbed to financial difficulties,\" to be succeeded by the Chicago Opera Company (1940–46). On December 6, 1936 — the alpha's month — the MGM starlet Betty Jaynes made her debut with the City Opera at fifteen. Opening night at the opera remained society's biggest single evening of the year; the boxes were the Social Register in tiers. The odd detail: The city's opera was reorganised out of bankruptcy twice in the decade; the boxholders stayed the same while the company's name changed under them.",
