      "summary": "Heinz Spanknöbel, authorised by Rudolf Hess in May 1933, formed the Friends of New Germany; he was deported in October 1933 for failing to register as a foreign agent, and his bodyguard was jailed that December for carrying a concealed weapon. The Friends had 5,000–10,000 members, mostly German citizens, and \"a strong presence\" in Chicago; Hess recalled its leaders in December 1935. The successor German American Bund was founded in Buffalo on March 19, 1936, under Fritz Kuhn, with about 25,000 members, divided into Gau Ost (40 local groups), Gau West (10) and Gau Midwest (19). Kuhn was convicted of embezzlement and tax evasion on December 5, 1939 (2½–5 years); the Bund was outlawed in December 1941. The odd detail: the Bund was founded not in New York but in Buffalo — at the Great Lakes' eastern door.",
