      "summary": "Chicago welcomed Italian air minister Italo Balbo and his transatlantic flying formation in July 1933. This was also a visit by a major Fascist official, a political fact that belongs beside the glamorous aviation story. Contemporary reporting placed his headquarters at the Drake and announced a thanksgiving Mass at Holy Name Cathedral, an afternoon with fair president Rufus Dawes and his wife, and a Stevens Hotel banquet for thousands of guests. An official reception schedule also lists a fair Casino ball and a Tavern Club dinner dance. Hotels, Catholic dignitaries, businessmen and politicians overlapped in the reception machinery.",
