      "summary": "Germany had no official pavilion, so a committee \"composed of leading Chicagoans of German descent\" built and ran a German-American building on the grounds. In July 1933 local Nazis (\"Friends of New Germany\" sympathisers) (unverified — V2_R04) demanded that the swastika flag fly over it. The committee \"absolutely refused the demand and decreed that as the exhibit was not an official government one, a swastika was not necessary\"; instead \"the committee is flying the imperial flag of Germany\" — the black-white-red of the Kaiser's Reich — over the building. The Chicago Daily Tribune ran \"Favor Imperial Flag for German Building at Fair\" (July 1933) and the Jewish Daily Bulletin \"Demand Swastika Fly on World Fair Bldg. Refused by Germans.\" (unverified — V2_R04) The German Consul General refused to intervene, and was recalled within weeks (next entry). The odd detail: In real 1933 Chicago the Kaiser's flag was the compromise flag — the one everybody could stand under. In this setting it is simply the flag of the winning power.",
