      "summary": "The culminating event of Jewish Day: a pageant of 3,000 years of Jewish history, produced by Meyer Weisgal of the Zionist Organization of America and directed by Isaac Van Grove on \"the largest stage ever constructed,\" with a cast variously counted at 3,000–6,000 (750 dancing girls, Roman legionaries and chariots, a 2,500-voice choir (unverified — V2_R04)), a Torah scroll on an altar at its centre, and 150,000 in the stands (per the Chicago Daily News), with 75,000 more at a repeat performance — \"top World's Fair attendance records.\" Dr. Chaim Weizmann came as keynote speaker; the Jewish Agency for Palestine sponsored it as a fundraiser, and the Daily News said its fellowship would \"carry rebuke to those who oppress the Jew\" in \"Hitler's Germany\". Weizmann wrote to his wife on 6 July: the day \"went off well… Everyone is praising the performance, though it was not to my taste.\" (unverified — V_R04) A Jewish Youth League tournament of 5,000–6,000 young athletes ran alongside. The pageant later toured. (A YouTube/archive.org clip circulating as a \"Moloch Baal ceremony at Soldier Field 1933\" is this pageant, mislabelled by conspiracy channels — useful as a period-style misreading.) The odd detail: The largest crowd of the whole fair was for a Jewish pageant with a Torah on an altar — and the internet's occultists still call it a Moloch rite.",
