      "summary": "On 10 July 1933 Vivian Chase of Kansas City, with Walter O'Malley and Percy \"Dice Box\" Fitzgerald, took the elderly Alton banker August Luer from his home and hid him \"in a damp underground cellar\" on a farm while they tried to collect a ransom. After 123 hours they let him go — because, the Vivian Chase page says, they feared he would die before any ransom came (his heart condition is not on that page). Chase's own end came on 3 November 1935: her body was found in a parked car at St. Luke's Hospital in Kansas City, shot in the neck with a .45, the bullet leaving through her chest. The odd detail: The kidnappers gave their victim back for nothing after five days, and the woman who took him was returned to a hospital car park two years later, dead.",
