      "synopsis": "Original note includes uncertainty or estimates: Cases began in June 1933 and were recognised as amoebic dysentery in mid-August; the peak ran 13 Aug–11 Oct. Between 1 June 1933 and 30 June 1934, 1,409 cases and 98 deaths were recorded, from \"over 400 cities scattered in 43 states, the Territory of Hawaii, and three Canadian Provinces\" — two-thirds of them out-of-town fairgoers; about 160,000 visitors had stayed at or eaten in the two hotels.",
