      "summary": "On 4 Aug 1933 Jarman, her lover George Dale and driver Leo Minneci robbed the shop of 71-year-old (unverified — V2_R06) Gustav Hoeh; in the struggle Dale shot him dead. The papers built Jarman — a mother of two, LeRoy and LaVerne — into \"the Blonde Tigress\" who had kicked the dying man (unverified — V2_R06); she got 199 years, Minneci 199, and Dale the chair. On 8 Aug 1940, aged 39, she climbed the wall at Dwight with fellow inmate Mary Foster and vanished. She was never caught — but she went to Sioux City, Iowa, to see that her children (raised by her sister Hattie Stocker) were all right, kept in touch with the family through coded classified ads, and in 1975 met her brother Otto Berendt, his wife and her son LeRoy in secret. A modern researcher (Silvia Pettem) argues she lived out her life as \"Marie Millman,\" a Denver waitress, dying in 1980. The odd detail: The most-wanted woman in Illinois (unverified — V2_R06) disappeared into the Depression's drift of the anonymous and was never caught — though her family saw her in secret as late as 1975 — the papers had already made her a beast, so they could not see a waitress.",
