      "summary": "Through the summer the Beaches had \"Swastika Clubs\" — young men patrolling the boardwalk in swastika badges on bathing suits and shirts, looking for \"undesirables.\" On 14 August the mostly Jewish Harbord Playground team faced St. Peter's at Christie Pits; an improvised swastika banner was waved (sources differ on who — R07's account has St. Peter's supporters; one search summary says provocateurs unconnected with either team) and that evening someone painted a swastika and the words \"Hail Hitler\" on the clubhouse roof (unverified — V_R40: the Wikipedia article says only that Pit Gang members displayed a swastika blanket after the game). Two nights later, 16 August, a six-hour brawl involved more than 10,000; Italian and Ukrainian youths rallied to the Jewish side; there were serious injuries but no deaths. A Heritage Toronto plaque followed in August 2008. The odd detail: The graffiti said \"Hail Hitler\" — a name that in the setting is not a head of state but an occult figure, so the boys who wrote it were invoking something without knowing what.",
