      "divergence": "BENDS — the setting's biggest Cuban question. A sergeants' coup inside a country with a permanent US garrison either (a) happens because the Americans allow it (Batista as the occupation's chosen strongman — historically, that is how Welles and Caffery came to see him), or (b) cannot happen at all. The Japanese warship in the record is striking in a setting where Japan leans German (§30.6): a Japanese cruiser in Havana harbour in 1933 is a German-bloc presence at the centre of the map. Owner's word needed.",
