      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the core; Medium on Lucy Sarber / Sharp specifics. • the wife/deputy detail comes from the general record and is UNVERIFIED on the pages read • The gang's impersonation of lawmen was a habit — the same trick (badges, credentials, \"we've come to move the prisoner\") recurs in the outlaw era, and it worked because a small-county sheriff's office in 1933 had no way to check (unverified — V2_R02) (at Lima it did not: Sarber asked for credentials and was shot).",
