      "summary": "Gus Winkler led the \"American Boys\", a crew of robbers and contract killers attached to Capone, and is a long-standing suspect in the St. Valentine's Day Massacre. He was accused over the September 1930 robbery of the Lincoln National Bank in Nebraska (almost $3 million, mostly bonds) and said he hadn't done it but knew who had. In the summer of 1933 he was seen visiting the Bankers Building office of Bureau of Investigation Special Agent in Charge Melvin Purvis, helping hunt Verne Miller after the Kansas City Massacre — which enraged Frank Nitti. On October 9, 1933, entering Weber's office, he was cut down by shotgun blasts from men hidden in the back of a green delivery truck. His wife Georgette later wrote memoirs. The odd detail: The killers waited inside a delivery truck parked at a beer distributor's — in the first autumn of legal beer.",
