      "summary": "On 13 November 1933 Peoria detectives (Detective Chief Fred Montgomery and Detective Robert Moran) questioned Russell Hughes, \"intimate friend of Klutas,\" in a barber shop; Hughes drew, two detectives were wounded and Hughes was shot dead. The same day three alleged gang members were under arrest in Chicago. On 24 November Klutas was indicted for counterfeiting $5 notes with Rex Howard, George Milligan and others. In the same fortnight — because the whole country was hunting kidnappers after the Brooke Hart abduction in San Jose (Hart's two killers were lynched on 26 Nov 1933) — Klutas's name was floated in the Hart case; the Hart kidnappers proved to be two local men and Klutas had nothing to do with it. The odd detail: a kidnapping gang whose second trade was printing money — the Secret Service's real jurisdiction (counterfeiting) reaches the gang before the police do.",
