      "summary": "On the evening of 21 Nov 1933, Dr. Alice Lindsay Wynekoop (b. 1 Feb 1871), a respected physician, child-welfare campaigner and Chicago clubwoman, said she had gone into her surgery at about 8:30 pm and found her daughter-in-law Rheta Gretchen Gardner Wynekoop (22, of Indianapolis) dead on the examination table in her basement surgery — shot with a .32 revolver, chloroformed, partly undressed. She phoned two of her children and the undertaker; it was the undertaker who, two hours later, called the police. Rheta's husband Earle had left Chicago at 10 that morning for a Grand Canyon photography trip and reached Kansas City about 12:30 a.m.; the investigation found he had \"courted\" more than fifty women. Ten days earlier (11 Nov) Alice had taken out a $5,000 double-indemnity policy on Rheta; she was deep in debt. After some seventy hours without sleep she told the coroner and the State's Attorney she had fired the gun after Rheta died under chloroform during an examination, having considered what would \"ease the situation best of all\" — then retracted. The first trial (Jan 1934) collapsed when her heart failed; the second convicted her on 6 Mar 1934 after 36 minutes. Twenty-five years; paroled Dec 1947; died 4 July 1955. The odd detail: The shot into a body that may already have been dead — a doctor's mercy on a corpse, or a staged burglary — in a surgery under the family house. Earle confessed falsely to protect his mother, then withdrew it. The jury foreman said in 1947 he thought someone else pulled the trigger.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High (Wikipedia case page is detailed and cited; Sun-Times feature agrees on the frame). • Catherine Wynekoop — Alice's daughter, also a physician, defended her (unverified — V2_R06).",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — The Wynekoop house is the perfect Chicago \"mad doctor\" set: a reform-minded lady physician, a cellar surgery, chloroform, a son with fifty women. Put a summoning under the surgery and the \"mercy shot\" becomes a binding.",
