      "summary": "Col. Frank Tompkins (b. 1868) — the major who chased the raiders out of Columbus and was shot at Parral — published Chasing Villa: The Story Behind the Story of Pershing's Expedition into Mexico in 1934: xx + 270 pages, maps on the endpapers, and an appendix (pp. 257–270) listing every commissioned officer who served with the Punitive Expedition. It was reviewed in the Hispanic American Historical Review (1936) and later reissued as Chasing Villa: The Last Campaign of the U.S. Cavalry. The odd detail: it is a period document published inside the campaign's decade — the Southern War's first-era veterans could buy their own war in a bookshop in 1934, with their officers' names in the back.",
