      "synopsis": "Industrialist Robert Ilg (Ilg Hot Air Electric Ventilating Co., Chicago) built Ilgair Park, a recreation park for his employees; its pools and artificial lake needed a big water tank and pumps, so in 1934 he hid them inside a 94-foot, half-size replica of the Leaning Tower of Pisa (architect Albert L. Farr). It contains five bells, three of them cast in Cavezzo, Italy in 1623, 1735 and 1747 — \"how they came to be…",
