      "summary": "Evelyn \"Billie\" Frechette, b. 15 Sept 1907 at Neopit on the Menominee reservation, French and Menominee by descent, was Dillinger's companion from the autumn of 1933 through Tucson, Crown Point, St. Paul and Mooresville. Arrested in Chicago on 9 April 1934, she was convicted under the new federal harboring law for hiding him in the St. Paul apartment and served two years at the federal farm at Milan, Michigan, released in 1936. She then toured for five years with Dillinger's father and family in a show called \"Crime Doesn't Pay,\" telling the story from a stage. She died of cancer at Shawano, Wisconsin, 13 Jan 1969, and is buried in Woodlawn Cemetery beside her third husband, Arthur Tic. The odd detail: The gangster's girl and the gangster's father toured the country together for five years, paid by the ticket (unverified — V2_R02), under a title the Bureau could have written.",
