      "summary": "The Silver Legion's uniform was a silver shirt with blue tie, campaign hat and blue corduroy trousers, with a scarlet \"L\" over the heart (\"Love, Loyalty, and Liberation\"). It claimed 15,000 members by 1934. Minnesota claimed about 6,000 members, some 800 in Minneapolis, where national field organiser Roy Zachary held rallies at the Royal Arcanum hall on July 29 and August 2, 1938, calling for a vigilante attack on Teamsters Local 544. Silver Shirt meetings in Chicago ended in riots in 1938 (Zachary was fined $15 for disorderly conduct), and in 1939 members smashed windows at the Goldblatt Brothers department store (Goldblatt's was a Jewish-owned Chicago chain). The odd detail: the national organiser of a would-be revolution was fined fifteen dollars in Chicago.",
