      "places": [
        {
          "name": "Chicago",
          "address": "",
          "geography": "(the Saint Germain Press; the Ballards' base) with \"conclaves\" in cities across the country from Philadelphia (Oct 1934) onward",
          "precision": "search locator, not surveyed",
          "map_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chicago%20%20with%20%22conclaves%22%20in%20cities%20across%20the%20country%20from%20Philadelphia%20%20onward"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Guy Ballard (writing as \"Godfré Ray King\") claimed that while hiking Mount Shasta in the early 1930s, looking for \"the Brotherhood of Mount Shasta,\" he met the Ascended Master Saint Germain. He and his wife Edna published Unveiled Mysteries (1934) and The Magic Presence (1935) through their own Saint Germain Press, and ran free public classes on the \"violet flame,\" the \"Mighty I AM Presence\" and the Ascended Masters (Jesus among them). A 1935 Los Angeles Shrine Auditorium class drew about 6,000; by 1938 the movement claimed up to a million followers. Guy Ballard died of arteriosclerosis in Los Angeles on 29 Dec 1939 and was cremated on the 31st; Edna and son Donald were indicted on eighteen counts of mail fraud in 1942, and United States v. Ballard (1944) became the Supreme Court's landmark on whether a jury may judge the truth of a religious belief. The odd detail: a Chicago mining promoter's mountain vision became, within four years, the largest new religious movement in the country — and its founder's death was, to believers, a failure to \"ascend.\"",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the outline; the Chicago street address and the Chicago venue for classes are not in the page (the Civic Opera House is often named — UNVERIFIED).",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — \"Cult versus population\": a million ordinary believers around a small Chicago core; the Ascended Masters are the period's reading, the \"violet flame\" the folklore — and what actually answered on Mount Shasta is the third layer. Section 13 opens a file the week the founder fails to ascend.",
