      "synopsis": "The fire of 19 May 1934 burned almost 90% of the yards — the Exchange Building, the Stock Yard Inn and the International Livestock Exposition building — for about $6 million, killed one employee and 8,000 cattle, and was seen from Indiana. The archive's H02 documents the cutting of electricity, gas and telephones in the district; this lane adds only the scale and the precedent: the 22–23 Dec 1910 stockyards fire…",
