      "divergence": "BENDS — Robert La Follette Sr.'s defining act was voting against U.S. entry into the Great War in April 1917 and surviving a Senate censure attempt (well-known; not re-verified on a page read this session); with America never entering, that fight does not exist, and the Progressive brand is a peace-and-farm brand without the war martyrdom. His 1924 Progressive run (a search result confirms he ran under the Progressive banner) would face President Leonard Wood in the setting — check the 1924 election. Philip's WWI army service (from memory, unverified here) would also bend.",
