      "summary": "Moran (b. 1895, Illinois; Tufts Medical) had practised in LaSalle until drink ruined him; in 1928 he was charged with first-degree murder after the death of 19-year-old Tillie Hartel in an abortion, took a plea, served time and lost his licence, then got parole in 1931 with a warden's help. Through a jewel thief he became \"the official physician of the Chicago Teamsters, Chauffeurs, Warehousemen and Helpers Union,\" set up on Irving Park Boulevard, and sold the underworld surgery. In March 1933 he operated on Fred Barker and Alvin Karpis for $1,250: the face work failed and was so painful Fred asked a friend to shoot him; the fingerprint removal on Karpis was so complete he later had trouble getting a passport. He laundered Bremer money. In a club outside Toledo, drunk, he told the gang, \"I have you guys in the palm of my hand,\" and disappeared in July 1934. On 26 September 1935 a body without hands or feet washed up at Crystal Beach, Ontario, and the Bureau matched its teeth to Moran. The accepted version is that Karpis and Fred Barker killed him on a boat ride on Lake Erie; Karpis himself said the Barker brothers shot him and buried him in a lime pit in Michigan. The odd detail: The man who took other men's fingerprints off was found without his hands — on the Canadian shore of a Great Lake, fourteen months later.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the record; the manner of death is genuinely disputed (two versions given).",
