      "summary": "Dillinger had been living since early July at the flat of Ana Cumpănaș — \"Anna Sage,\" a Romanian-born brothel-keeper from Gary and East Chicago now on Halsted Street — with her friend Polly Hamilton, a waitress, as his girl. Facing deportation, Sage went to the Bureau on 21 July through Sgt Martin Zarkovich of the East Chicago police, offering Dillinger for money and help with immigration. At 5:30 p.m. on Sunday 22 July she telephoned Melvin Purvis: the three would go to either the Biograph or the Marbro that evening. She wore orange (the press made it red). At 8:15 p.m. they went in to Manhattan Melodrama (Clark Gable, Myrna Loy, William Powell). More than twenty federal agents and five East Chicago officers took positions; Samuel Cowley ran the operation, Purvis stood by the box office to give the signal — he lit a cigar. At about 10:35 p.m. Dillinger came out, sensed the men closing, and broke for the alley; Charles Winstead fired three times, Clarence Hurt twice, Herman Hollis once. Four bullets hit: two grazed his face, one struck his left side, one entered the back of the neck, severed the spinal cord and came out under the right eye. Two women bystanders, Theresa Paulas and Etta Natalsky, were wounded. He had $7.70 in his pockets (standard record; UNVERIFIED on pages read). Souvenir hunters dipped handkerchiefs and newspapers in the blood on the pavement. An estimated 15,000 people filed past the body at the morgue in a day and a half; as many as four death masks were cast. Two sets of prints were taken at the scene and a third at autopsy; all were matched to the Dillinger card despite the acid work. The body went to Mooresville and then Maywood, Indiana, and into the ground at Crown Hill at 3:15 p.m. on 25 July. The odd detail: The Bureau's man of the hour gave the signal by lighting a cigar; the crowd took the blood home on their handkerchiefs; the Cook County Morgue became a public attraction for a day and a half after the Sunday-night shooting. Sage got $5,000 — half what she said she was promised — and was deported anyway.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High; the $7.70 and some crowd figures are from the standard record and marked. • standard record; UNVERIFIED on pages read",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — The owner's method already has the pieces: a real theatre, a real film, a real hour, a woman who chose the colour of her dress, fifteen thousand people who wanted to see the face. The occult layer is the morgue: four masks were cast from the face. Who has the fourth?",
