      "id": "R26-055",
      "title": "The Kerns Hotel fire — Lansing",
      "date_start": "1934-12-11",
      "date_end": "1934-12-11",
      "date_label": "11 December 1934",
      "category": "Detroit 1925–1940, in depth",
      "tags": [
        "Detroit",
        "depth",
        "Kerns Hotel",
        "Lansing"
      ],
      "people": [
        "the seven legislators named above"
      ],
      "places": [
        {
          "name": "the Kerns Hotel",
          "address": "",
          "geography": "100 block of North Grand Avenue, Lansing (beside the Grand River)",
          "precision": "search locator, not surveyed",
          "map_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=the%20Kerns%20Hotel%2C%20100%20block%20of%20North%20Grand%20Avenue%2C%20Lansing%2C%20Chicago"
        }
      ],
      "summary": "At about 5:30 a.m. on 11 December 1934 a fire, blamed on a carelessly dropped cigarette, swept the four-storey, 211-room, wood-interior hotel, which was full of legislators in town for a special session. Thirty-four died (32 at once, 2 later), among them seven members of the legislature: Senator John Leidlein and Representatives T. Henry Howlett, Charles D. Parker, Vern Voorhees, John W. Goodwine, Don E. Sias and D. Knox Hanna. A night janitor at a nearby newspaper saw the first flames on a second-floor curtain. Some guests jumped into the Grand River; spectators said \"many… did not see them resurface\". The hotel (built 1909) had been the first in Michigan with running ice water in every room. The odd detail: Seven lawmakers dead in one night, and men who jumped into the river and were never seen to come up.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — A special session, a hotel full of legislators, a fire at dawn — and bodies the river kept. If a bill was due to be voted that week, somebody wanted it dead.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Kerns Hotel fire — Wikipedia",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kerns_Hotel_fire",
          "publisher": "Wikipedia",
          "kind": "encyclopedia article (follow its citations for strong claims)",
          "supports": ""
        }
      ],
