      "unverified": [],
      "divergence": "BENDS — no Nazi Germany. The 1936 Games were awarded to Berlin in 1931 (real record) and in the setting a victorious Kaiser's Germany hosts them as the empire's showcase — the Reich that won the war, with Britain and France paying reparations, receiving the world. A Black American winning four golds in Imperial Berlin is a different story: not a rebuke to a racial state, but a colonial subject's champion (the American empire's) beating the Germans at their own festival, while Hitler is a fringe occultist somewhere in the crowd. The \"no snub\" detail travels well: the Kaiser (or whoever presides) does receive him — and the American press hates it.",
