      "summary": "Packard, the prestige make, launched the mid-priced One-Twenty in January 1935 at $980 (business coupe) to $1,095 (touring sedan) — its first entry into the competitive mid-price eight-cylinder market. It sold 24,995 that year against about 7,000 of all other Packards combined. For scale: the 1932 Ford V8 started at about $490 (R03). The odd detail: the \"cheap\" Packard cost twice a Ford — and still outsold every other Packard three to one.",
