      "summary": "On 5 May 1935 the Associated Filipino Press declared that the \"Philippine Uprising\" reported \"in the most sensational fashion\" by the Hearst papers — an incident in Laguna Province — was \"bunk,\" \"minor labor trouble … amongst the 'reds',\" spread \"merely to arouse prejudice to withhold independence.\" On 29 Dec 1935 the community split: the Filipino Association of Chicago (400 banqueters, 500 dancers) and the rival Associated Clubs held separate commemorations of the 39th anniversary of José Rizal's execution on the same night. On 26 Mar 1936 (printed April 1936) the Center debated \"Resolved, That American Occupation of the Philippines has Been a Blessing to the Filipinos\". The odd detail: Chicago Filipinos publicly denied a rebellion back home to protect a promise of independence.",
