      "summary": "Guiteras — born in 1906 in Bala Cynwyd, Pennsylvania, to a family with American ties — was the Hundred Days government's Interior Secretary, the man behind its minimum wage, labour laws and nationalisations (including the American-owned Cuban Electric Company). After Grau's fall he founded Joven Cuba, which preached armed \"direct action\". The March 1935 general strike was crushed by Batista. On 8 May 1935, waiting at El Morrillo for a boat to Mexico, Guiteras and the Venezuelan Carlos Aponte were killed in a gunfight with Batista's forces (the betrayal of the rendezvous is part of the standard account — UNVERIFIED on the page read). The odd detail: the most anti-American revolutionary of the decade was born a US citizen outside Philadelphia.",
