      "summary": "Addams died at 74 after surgery for an abdominal obstruction; doctors had found cancer in 1931 and never told her. First American woman to win the Nobel Peace Prize (1931, shared with Nicholas Murray Butler; she gave her share to the Women's International League for Peace and Freedom). The DAR had expelled her for pacifism after 1917. The 1913 \"Devil Baby\" legend — crowds besieging Hull House for weeks to see a horned, cloven-hoofed infant said to be hidden there, which Addams wrote up as a study in immigrant women's memory — is remembered, not on the page read. The odd detail: She was carried out of a house that, twenty-two years earlier, thousands of neighbours were certain held the Devil's child.",
