      "summary": "The Abendpost printed a directory of German societies. A sample: German-American Civic Association, 1545 Clybourn; Hanoverian Society, 3822 N. Neva; Palatinate Society at Lincoln Turner Hall; Rhenish Society at the Swiss Clubhouse; Saarlander Society, 1 N. LaSalle, Room 1244; Silesian Society at Manhattan Garden, 1517 Fullerton; Swabian Society (Schwaben Verein) at North Side Turner Hall; Thuringian Society at Richter's Hall; an Association of Russian-Germans; the United German-Austro-Hungarian Societies, 1412 Clybourn; Workmen's Singers at Mozart Hall, 1534 N. Clybourn; Social Turner Hall, 1653 Belmont; the Ferdinand La Salle Ladies' Chorus, 1638 N. Halsted; the Lorelei Ladies' Chorus, 2403 North Ave.; the Master Bakers' Wives' Chorus at Aldine Hall. The odd detail: the list includes a socialist \"Ferdinand Lassalle\" ladies' chorus, a Saarlander society meeting in a LaSalle Street office (Room 1244), and a Swabian club that has run a Cannstatter Volksfest every summer since 1878 (its 57th was in Aug 1934).",
