      "summary": "Twelve official victims (thought to be 7 men and 5 women), all decapitated — the head usually taken away — most also dismembered, several emasculated, several never identified. The first two were found together on 23 Sept 1935 at the base of \"Jackass Hill\" where E. 49th St dead-ends into the Run: Edward Andrassy (29, decapitated, emasculated, rope burns on the wrists, dead 2–3 days) and an unidentified man whose body had been soaked in oil and burned, hair shaved or scorched off. Florence Polillo (44) was found 26 Jan 1936 behind a business at 2315 E. 20th St, dismembered, wrapped in newspaper and packed in half-bushel baskets; her head was never found. The series ran through the \"Tattooed Man\" (June 1936), the Big Creek vagrant (July 1936), a bisected torso floating in a stagnant pool in Kingsbury Run near E. 37th (Sept 1936), the Euclid Beach torso (Feb 1937), Rose Wallace (June 1937), the Flats torso in a chicken-feed sack (July 1937), the morphine victim (Apr–May 1938), and the last pair, found on 16 Aug 1938 at the E. 9th St lakefront dump \"in plain view of\" Safety Director Eliot Ness's office windows at City Hall. Authorities questioned roughly 9,100 people. Nobody was ever tried; the case is officially open. The odd detail: Of the last two bodies (16 Aug 1938), the woman's was the rare one found with its head and hands (\"uncharacteristically,\" the cited page says) — dumped in a rag-and-cardboard bundle at the lakefront dump where Ness could look down on them from his window. Coroner Samuel Gerber's protocols note a \"surgical\" disarticulation at the third intervertebral disc, the same joint each time (unverified — V_R06).",
      "evidence_status": "research lead",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on dates, counts and locations (Encyclopedia of Cleveland History + Wikipedia victim table). Medium on Gerber's exact anatomical phrasing (from Wikipedia's summary of the protocols, not the protocols themselves). • Coroner Samuel Gerber's protocols note a \"surgical\" disarticulation at the third intervertebral disc, the same joint each time (unverified — V_R06).",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — The IHS seat at John Carroll University is a few miles up the hill from Kingsbury Run. Twelve bodies without heads over three years in the diocese where the order sits — either the order is hunting the Butcher, or it is quietly collecting the heads.",
