      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "Original note includes uncertainty or estimates: In nine autumn days two South Side teenagers terrorised the city. On 26 Oct 1935 Isador \"Idzi\" Rutkowski, 19, and Paul \"Shrimp\" Chovanec (EMKE spells it Chovonec), 16, set off a home-made bomb at the Shorewood Village Hall (damage, no dead); on 28 Oct they bombed two branches of the First Wisconsin National Bank; on 31 Oct — Halloween — two police precinct stations.",
