      "summary": "The Viator, a 232-ft Norwegian ocean freighter built at Stavanger in 1904 (983 GRT), was one of the small \"salties\" that came through the old canals into the lakes before the Seaway. Carrying pickled herring, she was rammed in heavy fog by the freighter Ormidale on 31 October 1935 and sank. (Crew fate and owner are not on the page read; standard accounts say all were taken off — UNVERIFIED.) She sits upright and largely intact except for the collision damage, in the Thunder Bay sanctuary. The odd detail: A Norwegian ship full of pickled herring on the bottom of Lake Huron on Hallowe'en — proof that ocean ships from Europe were on the lakes in the 1930s.",
