      "summary": "Walter Liggett edited the weekly Midwest American and accused senior Farmer-Labor politicians of collusion with Twin Cities organised crime, especially Isadore Blumenfeld, \"Kid Cann.\" On 9 December 1935, as he got out of his car carrying groceries, he was machine-gunned from a passing car while his wife Edith and daughter Marda watched. Edith identified Blumenfeld as the gunman, three other witnesses agreed, and the car belonged to Blumenfeld's associate Meyer Schuldberg — but Blumenfeld was acquitted and no one else was ever charged. The odd detail: Four eyewitnesses, including the widow, named the shooter — and a jury let him go.",
