      "summary": "Rebbe Aryeh Leib (\"Leibele\") Twerski was born in Hornosteipel on Hoshana Rabbah 1868, son of Rebbe Mordechai Dov and Rebbetzin Reitza, a daughter of the Divrei Chaim of Sanz; he was \"raised in the holy tradition of Chernobyl\" and descended from Rebbe Zusha of Hanipoli. \"In 1936, he went to Eretz Yisroel for one more year, and shortly thereafter\" immigrated to America, \"settling in Chicago,\" transplanting the Hornosteipel branch of the Chernobyl dynasty. His admirers wrote that \"the Twerski home in Chicago of those early days became an outpost of Torah and chassidus in the American wilderness,\" and that \"stories abound\" of his wonders (mofsim) — devotional stories, labelled as such. He died on 28 Teves 1951. The odd detail: Chicago's first resident rebbe of a great dynasty arrived only at the very end of the decade — the Old World court came to the city after almost everything else had.",
