      "summary": "The 380-ft whaleback Frank Rockefeller (built at Superior 1896 for $181,573.38, the 36th of 44 whalebacks) was sold in 1927 and became the sand dredge South Park; in 1936 she changed hands again and was converted to carry new automobiles from Detroit to Milwaukee and Kewaunee, which she did until she was wrecked off Manistique in 1942. Cleveland Tanker then rebuilt her as the tanker Meteor; she is the last whaleback afloat, a museum at Barker's Island, Superior. The odd detail: Detroit's cars crossing Lake Michigan in the belly of an 1896 steel whale — the decade's trade (cars, sand) using the last of the last century's oddest ships.",
