      "summary": "William \"Billy\" Mitchell, born in Nice on 29 Dec 1879, grandson of Alexander Mitchell (Scottish immigrant; the Milwaukee Road; the Marine Bank) and son of Senator John L. Mitchell (1883–89; the donor of Mitchell Park), grew up at Meadowmere (unverified — V_R27). Court-martialled in 1925 for calling the War and Navy departments' handling of air power \"almost treasonable,\" he resigned on 1 Feb 1926 and lived at Boxwood Farm, Middleburg, Virginia. He died in New York on 19 Feb 1936 at 56 and was buried at Forest Home; none of his children by his first marriage attended. The county airport was named for him in 1941. The odd detail: The prophet of the bomber was born on the Riviera to a Milwaukee railroad fortune and buried beside the brewers.",
