      "summary": "Reuters reported from Detroit that Virgil Effinger, \"described by the prosecution as the national head of the Black Legion\", had been indicted with 21 others for criminal syndicalism — \"advocating the teaching of crime, sabotage, violence or other forms of terrorism as a means of accomplishing industrial or political reforms\" — with a maximum of ten years and a $5,000 fine, plus a conspiracy count carrying five years. A few days after the exposure a Lima member told reporters the Legion's aim was legitimate and that its members wanted \"only to promote the best interests of America\". Imperial Wizard Hiram Evans \"indignantly denied\" any Klan affiliation (24 May). Isaac \"Peg-Leg\" White, a founding member, fled the syndicalism indictment and died of pneumonia in Maryland on 21 December 1936. R10 has Effinger's later life (the 1938 San Antonio \"Patriotic Legion\", death in a Toledo asylum 1955). The odd detail: The Klan's Imperial Wizard publicly disowned the Legion — the parent denying the child.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Confidence: High on the indictment's existence and terms; the outcome for Effinger (whether Ohio ever surrendered him to Michigan) is UNVERIFIED — I found no page that settled it.",
