      "summary": "Weather: 68°/56°, 1.37 in. of rain — the wettest day of the autumn. Sky: sunrise 5:56 am, sunset 5:19 pm CST (6:56 am / 6:19 pm on Chicago's EST clocks); waning crescent, 28%. In the papers: The Daily Banner (Greencastle, Ind.), 10 Oct 1936, p. 1: \"VOTERS HEAR GOV. LANDON AT CHICAGO\" — more than 25,000 in the Chicago Stadium, \"part of which stood in the rain outside\"; Landon on spending: \"put the spenders out\"; \"If I am elected the budget is going to be balanced not by depriving our needy relief…\"; introduced by M. J. Kennedy of the unions; \"He will leave Chicago at 11 p. m. after the address\" (Daily Banner, 9 Oct, p. 2). and . Same front page: \"ROOSEVELT DELIVERS MAJOR CAMPAIGN ADDRESS AT ST. PAUL\"; \"AROUND WORLD FLIER LANDS\"; \"PRESIDENT'S SON DENIES CHARGE\". National: Libeled Lady (MGM; Powell, Loy, Harlow, Tracy) released 9 Oct ( ); Boulder Dam began generating electricity. In the city: the Republican nominee's Chicago Stadium rally, 1800 W. Madison, with the overflow soaked on Madison Street. His running mate was a Chicagoan: Frank Knox, publisher of the Chicago Daily News since 1931 ( ).",
