      "summary": "Weather: 10th 65°/48°, 0.03; 11th 61°/44°; 12th 50°/44° (the first raw day); 13th 64°/47°. In the papers: 10 Oct — \"Typhoon struck Philippines killing at least 310.\" 11 Oct — the 175-day Arab general strike in Palestine ended; \"200 fascists attacked Jews in London's East End.\" 12 Oct — Soviet T-26 tanks landed at Cartagena; Dover–Dunkirk train ferry began. 13 Oct — Coronet magazine \"first published\" (Wikipedia's month page; the magazine's own page says the first issue, cover-dated November 1936, went on sale 23 Oct — see 23 Oct). In the city: Sat 10 — Northwestern 40, North Dakota Agricultural 7 (25,000 at Dyche); Notre Dame 14, Washington U. 6. Sun 11 — Bears 7, Cardinals 3 at Wrigley Field (16,288) — the city series. Mon 12 — Columbus Day (the Italian parade on the Near West Side is a fixture; 1936 details UNVERIFIED). Pacelli was in Boston 12–15 Oct with Bishop Spellman (Wikipedia, 1936 visit).",
