      "summary": "Weather: 15th 74°/53°; 16th 76°/51°, 0.09; 17th 51°/40° — the first cold snap. Sky: new moon Thu 15 Oct, 4:21 am — dark nights through the weekend. In the papers: 15 Oct — \"British press self-censored Simpson divorce coverage while U.S. made it front-page news\"; Pacelli back in New York from Boston. 16 Oct — \"American newspapers disappeared from British newsstands\" (the pages about the King cut out); Siege of Oviedo ended. 17 Oct — Decatur Daily Democrat, p. 3: \"Ford Host to Landon in Detroit\" ( ). In the city: Sat 17 — Northwestern 14, Ohio State 13 at Dyche (35,000); Notre Dame 27, Wisconsin 0. In release: Dimples (Shirley Temple), Daniel Boone, 15 Maiden Lane (all 16 Oct). Radio: Saturday night was the WLS National Barn Dance from the Eighth Street Theatre (since 1931; on NBC since 1933; the only radio show that charged admission — \"audiences would stand outside in the snow and cold waiting to get in\"; Lulu Belle and Scotty, the Hoosier Hot Shots, Red Foley, Pat Buttram — ).",
