      "summary": "Weather: 66°/40°. In the city: David E. Shanahan, many-times Speaker of the Illinois House and Bridgeport's man in Springfield since the 1890s, died in Chicago on 18 October 1936 — \"just a few weeks before the general election with his name still on the ballot.\" The vacancy went, on 3 Nov, to a 34-year-old Bridgeport clerk named Richard J. Daley, who \"had technically won the Republican nomination\" by write-in because Democratic rules capped Bridgeport's nominees, then \"immediately joined the House Democratic Caucus upon his taking office in Springfield in January 1937.\" Shanahan's estate \"exceeded one million dollars\" and went into litigation \"when his secret marriage to a secretary was revealed.\" Also: Bears 26, Pittsburgh 7 at Wrigley (20,000), 5–0. Cansiglio earthquake in Italy; Nationalists took Illescas.",
