      "id": "R24-013",
      "title": "Sun 25 October — PACELLI'S GREAT LAKES DAY: South Bend, then Chicago (the feast of Christ the King)",
      "date_start": "",
      "date_end": "",
      "date_label": "Sun 25 October",
      "category": "October 1936",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 53°/34°, 0.48 in. of rain — the Scholastic calls it \"threatening weather\"; the rain came with a falling thermometer (34° on the 26th's morning, then a 34°/31° day). Sky: sunrise 6:14 am, sunset 4:54 pm CST; waxing gibbous, 73%, moonrise 2:05 pm, on the meridian 7:51 pm, moonset 1:48 am on the 26th (USNO; the 12:37 am set on the 25th is the previous night's moon) — and on Chicago's EST clocks every one of these is an hour later: sunrise 7:14, sunset 5:54, moonrise 3:05 pm, moonset 2:48 am — so the Chicago evening had a bright moon behind the cloud. - Hour by hour (Notre Dame Scholastic, 30 Oct 1936, \"Eugenio Cardinal Pacelli Is Awarded Honorary Doctorate of Letters at Special Convocation\", pp. 3 and 23 — ): \"Flying from New York in a specially chartered plane, the visiting cardinal arrived at the Bendix airport in South Bend Sunday afternoon at 2 o'clock.\" Met by Rev. John F. O'Hara, C.S.C. (president), Very Rev. James W. Donohue, C.S.C. (superior-general of Holy Cross), Bishop John F. Noll of Fort Wayne and Bishop Joseph Ritter of Indianapolis. \"Cardinal Pacelli and his party proceeded by automobile through South Bend to the University where they were met by the student band … warmly cheered by the student body lining the route.\" A brief prayer at Sacred Heart Church \"with the faculty assembled in cap and gown\"; he gave the papal blessing; then Washington Hall, where Rev. J. Leonard Carrico read the citation: \"The University of Notre Dame at this special convocation of the faculty on the great feast of Christ the King is most happily privileged in announcing the conferring of the degree of doctor of letters, honoris causa, on: A prince of the Church … an ecclesiastical statesman and diplomat who in an era of world conflict has done much toward the conciliation of warring peoples…\" O'Hara spoke of Notre Dame as \"The City of the Blessed Sacrament.\" \"After a brief talk in which he thanked the University for its warm welcome, Cardinal Pacelli gave the benediction of the Holy Father. Despite threatening weather the Cardinal and his party left immediately for the Bendix airport to go to Chicago where His Eminence was the overnight guest of George Cardinal Mundelein.\" He also granted the students a holiday (they polled on whether to take the Friday after Thanksgiving or an extra day at Christmas — Scholastic p. 4). The Indianapolis Times (26 Oct, p. 2, \"NOTRE DAME HONORS CARDINAL PACELLI\"): \"received the doctor of letters degree … yesterday afternoon … the highest Catholic official ever to visit this country, left by plane for Chicago where he was to meet with Cardinal Mundelein, archbishop of Chicago.\" Chicago, Sunday night: Pacelli was Mundelein's overnight guest. Where is UNVERIFIED this session — the cardinal's town residence was 1555 N. State Parkway (general knowledge); his country seat was the villa at St. Mary of the Lake Seminary, Mundelein, Ill. Wikipedia's air-tour city list puts Cleveland on the route too, but the Indianapolis itinerary begins at South Bend; Cleveland may have been a fuel stop or on the return leg — UNVERIFIED. Also that day: Bears 12, Detroit Lions 10 at Wrigley (27,424), 6–0. Rome–Berlin Axis pact signed (Wikipedia, October 1936). Rexist march on Brussels fizzled.",
      "evidence_status": "research lead",
      "uncertainties": "Imported original calendar research; retain estimates, missing observations and time-zone caveats in the source.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — this is the owner's own method — he \"extended the actual cardinal inviting him.\" The real Pacelli slept in Chicago on the night of 25 Oct 1936 under Mundelein's roof, with rain on the windows and a bright moon behind the cloud. IHS's American province (John Carroll, outside Cleveland) is 350 miles east; South Bend and Chicago are the two stops where the Church's number two could be quietly briefed. The FBI's Section 13 would want the guest list; the Secret Service, its rival, would want the airport.",
