      "summary": "Weather: 1st 67°/51°, 0.05; 2nd 67°/60°, 0.39 in. (a warm, wet Monday). In the papers: 1 Nov — Mussolini's Milan speech on a \"German-Italian axis.\" 2 Nov — the BBC Television Service opened in London; the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation began (across the lake). In the city: Sun 1 — Green Bay 21, Bears 10 at Wrigley Field before 31,346, the biggest football crowd in Chicago all season; the Bears' first loss. All Saints' Day (holy day) — every parish full. The Tribune's pre-election countdown (its famous switchboard greeting, \"only X days left to save your country\") is general knowledge, not re-checked this session.",
