      "summary": "Weather: 53°/30°. In the papers: \"Peel Commission arrived in Palestine; Joseph Goebbels banned art criticism in Germany; Roosevelt sent birthday greetings to Victor Emmanuel III.\" In the city: the real Chicago observed Armistice Day with the two-minute silence at 11 am, parades and Soldier Field/Loop ceremonies (general; 1936 particulars UNVERIFIED). - Divergence note: BENDS HARD. America never entered the Great War, so 11 November is not an American holiday in the setting; there is no Unknown Soldier, no Legion parade, no poppies. Europe's armistice (Germany's victory) is a foreign anniversary; the German community of the North Side might mark it, and the Poles and Czechs would not. Goebbels does not exist; Palestine is Ottoman.",
      "evidence_status": "research lead",
      "uncertainties": "Imported original calendar research; retain estimates, missing observations and time-zone caveats in the source.",
