      "date_label": "Thu 12 – Sat 14 November",
      "category": "November 1936",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 12th 53°/36°; 13th 50°/35°; 14th 55°/39°. Sky: new moon Fri 13 Nov, 10:42 pm. In the papers: 12 Nov — the San Francisco–Oakland Bay Bridge opened; Churchill attacked the government over German rearmament. 13 Nov — fist-fight in the French Chamber over Salengro; Go West, Young Man (Mae West) released. 14 Nov — \"Germany announced it would not observe Treaty of Versailles river articles\"; Durruti reached Madrid. In the city: Thu 12 — Black Hawks' home opener at the Chicago Stadium, 0–0 with the Americans. Sat 14 — Northwestern 9, Michigan 0 at Ann Arbor (28,295); Notre Dame 20, Army 6 at Yankee Stadium (74,423); Black Hawks lost 2–6 at Toronto. Theodora Goes Wild (Irene Dunne) released 12 Nov.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
