      "summary": "Weather: 18th 39°/28°; 19th 36°/20°; 20th 59°/35°. In the papers: 18 Nov — \"On 18 November 1936, [USS Indianapolis] embarked Roosevelt … at Charleston, South Carolina, and conducted a goodwill cruise to South America\" (Rio, Buenos Aires, Montevideo; back at Charleston 15 Dec — ); \"Italy and Germany recognized Francoist Spain\"; Edward VIII at Dowlais: \"something must be done.\" 19 Nov — Duff Cooper on conscription. 20 Nov — Akita dike collapse killed 362; Durruti and José Antonio Primo de Rivera died; Love on the Run (Gable, Crawford) released. Great Lakes: the Bendix sit-down at South Bend — about 1,200 workers sat down inside the Bendix Products plant from about 18 Nov; Indiana papers ran it daily through the 25th (\"Harmony Reigns at Bendix 'Sit Down' Strike\"; union and company conferences in South Bend) — 14 articles in the Indianapolis Times, Decatur Daily Democrat and Daily Banner, 18–25 Nov 1936 (Hoosier State Chronicles search \"Bendix strike South Bend\"; end date UNVERIFIED). This was the UAW's first big sit-down, six weeks before Flint. In the city: Thu 19 — the Black Hawks lost to the Montreal Maroons at the Stadium.",
