      "id": "R24-031",
      "title": "Thu 26 November — THANKSGIVING",
      "date_start": "",
      "date_end": "",
      "date_label": "Thu 26 November",
      "category": "November 1936",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 26°/16° — the coldest day so far; a bitter, dry holiday. Sky: sunrise 6:53 am, sunset 4:22 pm; moon 94%, rising 2:42 pm — a near-full moon over the dinner table. In the city: the Bears lost 7–13 at Detroit in the Lions' Thanksgiving game (22,000) — with the Cardinals' win three days later it cost them the division; the Black Hawks beat Detroit 2–0 at the Olympia for their first win of the year. The Daily Mirror put Mrs. Simpson on its front page in London. The State Street Christmas parade (the \"State Street Christmas Parade\", begun as the \"Christmas Caravan\" on 7 Dec 1934 by the State Street Council, \"to stimulate holiday shopping and improve public morale\") was by 1935 pulled along the trolley tracks by an old streetcar; its 1936 date is UNVERIFIED — .",
