      "id": "R24-032",
      "title": "Fri 27 – Sat 28 November — the Stock Show opens under a full moon",
      "date_start": "",
      "date_end": "",
      "date_label": "Fri 27 – Sat 28 November",
      "category": "November 1936",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 27th 33°/14°; 28th 44°/25°. Sky: full moon Sat 28 Nov, 10:12 am (the full moon before the eclipse moon). In the papers: 27 Nov — Roosevelt at Rio; the British cabinet rejected the morganatic plan. 28 Nov — Navy 7, Army 0; Franco's secret treaty with Italy; Ecuador's army revolt; Born to Dance (Eleanor Powell, James Stewart, Cole Porter's \"I've Got You Under My Skin\") released 27 Nov. In the city: Sat 28 Nov — the 37th International Live Stock Exposition opened at the International Amphitheatre at the Union Stock Yards (\"Agriculture's biggest show\" in its \"$2,000,000\" hall — Decatur Daily Democrat 20 Nov p. 5; Nappanee Advance-News 26 Nov p. 4; Indianapolis Times 25 Nov p. 2 and 2 Dec p. 5, corn awards; 4-H winners pictured 2 Dec — Hoosier State Chronicles search \"International Live Stock\"). The Amphitheatre had opened in 1934 after the fire that burned the old one and blacked out the district (the Codex archive's H02/H03). Farm families from five states filled the Stock Yard Inn and the South Side hotels for the week.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Imported original calendar research; retain estimates, missing observations and time-zone caveats in the source.",
