      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 39°/2°, 0.05 in. — the high came early and the bottom fell out; by dawn on the 7th it was 2° above zero. In the city: Betty Jaynes, 15, made her debut with the Chicago City Opera Company on 6 December 1936 ( ) — \"a 'sensational debut' … in La bohème\" ( ; the role, presumably Mimì, is not named on the page). Three days later a Chicago probate judge approved her MGM contract (see 9 Dec). The company (1935–39, at the Civic Opera House) was in its autumn season — the baritone Stefano Ballarini had made his American debut with it in October (Wikipedia search snippet). Black Hawks lost 1–2 to the Rangers at the Stadium. Mexico said Trotsky could enter.",
      "evidence_status": "documented",
      "uncertainties": "Imported original calendar research; retain estimates, missing observations and time-zone caveats in the source.",
