      "summary": "Weather: 8th 40°/19°; 9th 42°/29° — the cold broke. In the papers: 8 Dec — the battleship Gneisenau launched; Ossietzky barred from Oslo; Nicaraguan elections. 9 Dec — the British cabinet \"pleaded with Edward to reconsider\"; a KLM airliner crashed at Croydon killing 15 of 17, among them the autogiro's inventor Juan de la Cierva; Lottie Pickford died. In the city: Tue 8 — the Immaculate Conception, a holy day of obligation: Holy Name Cathedral and every parish full at the morning Masses. Black Hawks 0–0 at the Rangers. Wed 9 — \"On December 9, 1936, Probate Judge John F. O'Connell in Chicago approved Jaynes' contracts with MGM and a concert booking company\" — \"$250 to $1,300 per week plus additional payments when she made films\" ( ).",
