      "id": "R24-040",
      "title": "Fri 11 December — \"the woman I love\"",
      "date_start": "",
      "date_end": "",
      "date_label": "Fri 11 December",
      "category": "December 1936",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 22°/11° — hard cold again. Sky: sunrise 7:08 am, sunset 4:20 pm (the earliest sunset of the year, 11–13 Dec); a 5% crescent moon rising 5:04 am. In the papers: \"His Majesty's Declaration of Abdication Act received Royal Assent\"; on the night of 11 December (London time) Edward, introduced by Sir John Reith as \"His Royal Highness Prince Edward,\" broadcast from Windsor Castle that he could not carry the burden \"without the help and support of the woman I love.\" London's night is Chicago's afternoon; the broadcast hour is not on the pages read this session (the usual figure, 10 pm GMT, would be 4 pm in Chicago — UNVERIFIED here). Also: an amendment to the Irish Free State constitution removed the King from its internal affairs; General Spanky released. ; In the city: every radio in the Loop on at once in mid-afternoon — the networks carried the BBC feed. Radio that night: it was a Friday; the Chicago-made NBC shows of the week were Fibber McGee and Molly (from WMAQ, on NBC Red \"from 1936 on,\" sponsored by Johnson's Wax — ), Amos 'n' Andy (nightly, Pepsodent; made at NBC's Merchandise Mart studios until the move west — ), and on Wednesdays after 11 pm Lights Out — WENR's horror show, written since June 1936 by Arch Oboler, whose first script, \"Burial Services\" (\"a paralyzed girl who gets buried alive\"), drew \"over 50,000 complaint letters\" and got the show banned from the air before 11 pm; his follow-ups that season were \"Catwife\" (\"a woman who turns into a giant feline\") and \"The Dictator\" ( ).",
      "evidence_status": "research lead",
      "uncertainties": "Imported original calendar research; retain estimates, missing observations and time-zone caveats in the source.",
      "hook": "Proposal, not canon — Lights Out is the setting's own genre, made in Chicago, on the air at midnight on Wednesdays in the very month of the alpha. A GM can put the players' radio on WENR.",
