      "summary": "Weather: 48°/26°, dry. In the city: Clarence Herschberger, 60 — Amos Alonzo Stagg's fullback and kicker, \"the first western player to be selected as a first-team All-American, in 1898\" — was found dead in the basement of his home on W. 64th Street. \"He had connected a rubber hose to a laundry gas burner and had inhaled illuminating gas.\" His daughter Ruth, 19, found him. Ruled suicide; he \"had suffered a nervous breakdown four years before he died, and had suffered from heart disease,\" and was despondent after leaving the real-estate business. . Also: David Frankfurter sentenced to 18 years in Switzerland for shooting the Nazi Gustloff; the cruiser Canarias sank the Soviet Komsomol.",
