      "summary": "Weather: 38°/16°, dry. A clear-cold day by the numbers: a 22-degree spread means little cloud; the low of 16° came before dawn on the 23rd. Sky: sunrise 7:15 am, sunset 4:23 pm, civil twilight 6:44 am / 4:55 pm; waxing gibbous moon, 64% lit, risen at 12:02 pm, on the meridian at 6:57 pm, setting at 2:04 am on the 23rd (USNO; the 12:51 am set listed for the 22nd is the previous night's moon) — a half-and-more moon high in the south at suppertime, gone by a little after two in the morning. Six nights to the full moon and the eclipse. (USNO: ) In the papers: \"Egyptian parliament ratified Anglo-Egyptian treaty\" ( ). Three days to Christmas; the Loop at its most crowded; the State Street windows lit by half past four. In the city: the Black Hawks lost 1–4 at Montreal. Radio that night (a Tuesday): the NBC and CBS Chicago originations; WGN's nightly hour from the Aragon ballroom on Lawrence Avenue (\"Each night, powerhouse radio station WGN broadcast an hour-long program from the hall\" — ).",
