      "summary": "For 44 days UAW members occupied the Fisher Body plants that made the dies for GM's car bodies. On 11 January 1937 police tried to retake Fisher Body 2; strikers drove them off with hinges, bottles and bolts — 14 were wounded by gunfire — and named it \"the Battle of the Running Bulls.\" Genora Johnson (later Dollinger) organised the all-female Emergency Brigade. Governor Frank Murphy refused to use force against the strikers and sent the National Guard to protect them from police and company guards. GM recognised the UAW; its membership grew from 30,000 to 500,000 within a year. The odd detail: A governor who deployed the Guard to protect strikers — the opposite of Toledo 1934 and Chicago 1937.",
