      "summary": "In 1937 President Lázaro Cárdenas decreed an agrarian reform that turned the henequen haciendas into collective ejidos, leaving the former owners only 150 hectares each for private use; the plantations \"ceased to exist as autonomous communities.\" The decree fulfilled, fourteen years late, what Carrillo Puerto had legislated between 28 November and 4 December 1923. A scholarly book on the reform is titled Cárdenas Compromised: The Failure of Reform in Postrevolutionary Yucatán (Ben Fallaw, Duke University Press — title via search). The odd detail: the same hacienda buildings that had held slaves now became — as many still are — ruins, hotels and museums.",
