      "synopsis": "Weather: 12th 37°/20°; 13th 49°/23°, 0.23 in. — \"January 13–24: Near record rainfalls were recorded\" across the Ohio valley; the rain that made the Ohio River flood of 1937 began this day (Cincinnati would reach 80 ft on the 26th; 385 dead, a million homeless; Shawneetown, Ill., moved three miles inland afterwards — ). Sky: new moon Tue 12 Jan, 10:47 am.",
