      "title": "Thu 14 – Fri 15 January — snow at last",
      "date_start": "",
      "date_end": "",
      "date_label": "Thu 14 – Fri 15 January",
      "category": "January 1937",
      "tags": [
        "R24",
        "calendar"
      ],
      "people": [],
      "places": [],
      "summary": "Weather: 14th 48°/26°, 0.04 in., 0.1 in. snow; 15th 26°/12°, 0.7 in. of snow — the first real snowfall since 5 December, on the last day of the window. In the papers: 14 Jan — the Paul Bunyan and Babe statues unveiled at Bemidji, Minnesota (northwoods folklore made concrete); Göring with Mussolini and Ciano in Rome. 15 Jan — Blum given power to stop volunteers to Spain; the Second Battle of Corunna Road ended; Frederick Richardson, the Chicago illustrator (Queen Zixi of Ix, the Daily News art department), died (Wikipedia search snippet). In the city: Thu 14 — Black Hawks lost 3–7 at the Maroons (season record to date 6–12–6; they finished 14–27–7, \"in the cellar of the American Division,\" Clem Loughlin coaching, Major Frederic McLaughlin owning — ). Just past the window (for a GM who runs on): 17/27 Jan — Warner Bros.' Black Legion, Humphrey Bogart as a Midwestern machinist who joins the hooded order (Wikipedia's month page says premiered 17 Jan; the film's page says New York premiere 27 Jan, general release 30 Jan) — ; 18 Jan — the Ohio at Cincinnati passed 52 ft; 20 Jan — Roosevelt's second inauguration, the first ever held on 20 January, in pouring rain; 25 Jan — The Guiding Light began on NBC from Chicago (general knowledge); 11 Feb — Flint settled.",
