      "summary": "Parish priest of Santa Isabel since 1924, Maldonado worked in hiding under Chihuahua's priest limits. On Ash Wednesday, 10 February 1937, drunk armed men found him; he snatched up the pyx of consecrated hosts as he was dragged out by the hair to the local boss Andrés Rivera, who struck him on the head with a pistol, fracturing his skull and destroying an eye. The pyx fell open; one of them picked up the hosts and told the priest, \"Eat this!\" Local women got him taken to Chihuahua City, where he died on 11 February. Canonized 21 May 2000; the Diocese of El Paso honours him. The odd detail: the host forced into a dying priest's mouth by his killer.",
