      "summary": "Opened in 1898 as the largest steel arch bridge in the world, the Honeymoon Bridge was destroyed when a wind-driven ice floe from Lake Erie jammed the gorge; the water and ice rose to a record, well above the 1909 mark. Officials thought reinforcement might save it, but by the afternoon inspectors heard rivets snapping; the workers ran, the arch buckled, and the bridge fell into the river in four pieces. No one was killed. The Rainbow Bridge replaced it. The odd detail: The engineers heard it going — rivets snapping like gunfire — before anyone saw it move.",
