      "divergence": "BENDS — the single hardest bend in the lane. Tampico and the Golden Lane are the TAMPICO ENCLAVE, American-held: Mexico cannot expropriate oil it does not hold. Options: (a) a 1938 expropriation of the oil outside the enclave (Poza Rica, discovered 1930, is south in Veracruz state — in the setting the one great field Mexico kept?) — a defiant nationalisation beside an American enclave that cannot touch it; (b) a demand under Article 27 that the enclave's oil is Mexican — a diplomatic crisis instead of a nationalisation; (c) a strike in the enclave. Recommend (a) + (b) together; Britain (defeated, broke) cannot protest in the setting, and Germany might buy the nationalised oil — as a German-won world's Europe would. Veracruz's customs receivership sits right between the two.",
