          "label": "Jamaica — status proposal (historical sense, not a ruling)",
          "text": "the largest and most populous British island and the hardest to sell — a colony of a million people with its own Legislative Council, a Kingston merchant class and the empire's Caribbean garrison. Proposal: still British, with an American naval lease on the south coast (Portland Bight / Old Harbour — the site the 1940 deal chose) from c. 1920. Keeping Jamaica British keeps Garvey's deportation (1927), Howell's trial (1934) and the 1938 rising as recorded, and makes Kingston the setting's \"foreign port inside the American lake\". The alternative (bought outright) is noted above entry by entry."
