      "synopsis": "At the Évian Conference on Jewish refugees (July 1938), the Dominican Republic was the only country to offer to take large numbers — up to 100,000. In 1940 Trujillo donated about 26,000 acres at Sosúa; in the end about 800 German and Austrian Jews received visas (1940–45) and founded a settlement whose dairy firm, Productos Sosúa, still exists, with a synagogue and museum.",
