      "summary": "The joining of the spans was celebrated coast to coast by radio on 28 May 1938; Governor Frank Murphy and Ontario Premier Mitchell Hepburn dedicated the $3.25 million bridge on 8 October 1938 with 30,000 people walking across, fireworks, banquets, boat parades and a Port Huron parade. The same autumn the Public Works Administration declared dead (1 November) the application for a $25–30 million bridge at the Straits of Mackinac, and on 12 December rejected a proposed $40 million Detroit subway. The odd detail: In one season Michigan got a bridge to Canada and was refused a bridge between its own peninsulas and a subway under its biggest city.",
