      "summary": "Richard Reading, mayor from 4 January 1938 (he had ordered all city departments to hunt out Communists on 14 October 1938), sold protection to numbers operators and promotions to police officers. In 1940 a grand jury indicted a slate of officials on graft charges — Wayne County Prosecutor Duncan C. McCrea (the man who had prosecuted the Black Legion), Mayor Reading, Wayne County Sheriff Thomas C. Wilcox (who, as police commissioner in 1930, had produced the affidavit calling the murdered Jerry Buckley an extortionist) and Police Superintendent Fred Frahm. Reading got four to five years and served three. Meanwhile, on 13 December 1938, the Black Legion's Roy Hepner — a leader of the Kingsley murder plot — was released from prison after two years. The odd detail: The prosecutor who broke the Black Legion and the commissioner who smeared Buckley ended in the same indictment.",
