      "summary": "Carl Zeidler (b. Milwaukee 4 Jan 1908; Marquette 1929, law 1931; assistant city attorney 1936–40) beat the 24-year mayor Daniel Hoan in April 1940 with \"elaborate campaign shows\" — balloons released from ceilings — devised by Robert Bloch and Harold Gauer, whose promised salaries never came. Zeidler served 15 April 1940–8 April 1942, resigned to join the Navy, commanded the gun crew on the merchantman La Salle, and vanished with her on 7 Nov 1942 when U-159 sank her; he was declared dead on 11 Dec 1944 at 34 and has a cenotaph at Forest Home. His brother Frank, a Socialist, took City Hall in 1948. The odd detail: The mayor who ended the Socialists' quarter-century was elected by two pulp writers' stagecraft and has no grave.",
