      "synopsis": "Folklore account: The first major slide was at Cucaracha — the first crack noted 4 October 1907, about 400,000 cubic metres (500,000 cubic yards) of clay; Gaillard called the slides \"tropical glaciers, made of mud instead of ice.\" On 18 September 1915 two massive slides closed the canal for nearly seven months, its longest closure. From 1915 to 2000 the cut was named the Gaillard Cut after Maj.",
