      "summary": "The legend says Jesuits worked a rich silver mine at a hidden town Guadalupe de Tayopa and, when the order was suppressed, hid it. J. Frank Dobie gave Tayopa a chapter in Apache Gold and Yaqui Silver (1939). A search summary adds that a Jesuit inventory sealed 17 February 1646 was reportedly found by Henry O. Flipper in 1912 — the first Black graduate of West Point, who became a mining-law and land expert in Mexico — and that in 1927 Dobie and C. B. Ruggles were shown a longer copy with directions from \"Mesa Campanero.\" (Not confirmed from a primary source.) The odd detail: the treasure map's alleged finder is Henry O. Flipper, and the storyteller who put it in print is J. Frank Dobie — a Texas folklorist who was at the camp in Chihuahua in 1927.",
