      "collection": "Chicago & Great Lakes",
      "synopsis": "Folklore account: Of the Kamloops' 22 crew (lost about 7 December 1927), nine bodies were found — five identified and four not; the four unidentified were finally buried at Thunder Bay in 2011. The wreck still holds human remains, including a crewman lodged under a stairway in the engine room whom divers call \"Old Whitey\" (some accounts \"Grandpa\"), preserved by the cold.",
