      "summary": "A stone angel at the Deere tomb became the town's bravery test: teenagers ran through the cemetery at the stroke of midnight and touched it. Legend says it was a white marble statue that turned black after a lightning strike (a second story says a Black child was chained to it by tormentors and lightning struck in judgment); other tales have a young man die of a heart attack on touching it and a young woman found unconscious with her hair gone white after a night in the cemetery. The statue was later removed to stop vandalism; one account says it went to a retreat centre in New Mexico, a reader's comment says the Moline fire department kept it under a cover. The odd detail: The Deere family's own angel is the local ghost — the plough king's monument is Moline's haunt.",
